{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/380264-so-if-lunars-can-t-use-ma-in-animal-forms-divine-person-forms-vs-divine-beast-forms","id":380264,"title":"So, if Lunars can't use MA in animal forms... [divine person forms VS divine beast forms]","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Lunar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-01-24T10:30:50-08:00","id":380264,"title":"So, if Lunars can't use MA in animal forms... [divine person forms VS divine beast forms]","content":"Lunars can't use Evocations in war form, and cannot use Martial Arts Charms in sufficiently inhuman forms* when the Styles were designed for humans; because animal shapes can't use human Martial Arts even when the animal is really a Lunar.<br /> <br /> [lightly joking] At this point, I'm wondering what forms lock Lunars out of sorcery! [/lightly joking]<br /> <br /> <br /> * Technically, Morke and Holden are saying &quot;animal forms&quot;, but I figure that Dragon Kings can still practice just about any human-made Style, because there's been no word that DBT locks out martial arts. Tails and digitigrade feet notwithstanding, I think there's more alike between the upright posture of a human and a dragon king than between a human and a gorilla. (Though just as cranes can't practice the human-designed Crane Style, humans definitely have worse odds of ever practicing the Pterok-designed Dagger Wing Style than cranes do.)<br /> <br /> <br /> Now, I don't have a problem with this, and I'll explain why in terms of Fluff and Crunch.<br /> <br /> In terms of fluff, humans designed Snake Style to be a range of human movements that took inspiration from snake movements, but which keep in mind that the human has arms and legs and does not slither on the ground. Because a snake does not have arms and legs, a snake is better off fighting like a snake as it always did before, rather than pretending to be a human (with limbs it does not have) pretending to be a snake (with limbs it should not have). Why go through a middleman when the snake is already where it wants to be?<br /> <br /> In terms of crunch, we know that animals are going to have unique-ish abilities that they can unlock with XP. Familiars can learn these tricks under the guidance of Exalted masters and Lunars can learn them after taking the creature's Heart's Blood and assuming its form. These abilities represent a snake mastering fighting like a snake (rather than like a human failing badly at being a snake), and represent a potentially competitive option for Lunars as an alternative to Snake Style. Especially since those snake abilities can be made as strong as they can and should be without any consideration of how they might have been too powerful in combination with Snake Style Charms.<br /> <br /> <br /> So, there's no need for panic, and instead, there's cause for celebration. Because this means that those Lunar players who want to invest more into their various animal forms for a stronger Beast Boy fighting style can be assured that they will have the option to do so without needing to master multiple Martial Arts Styles (and design several more for the forms that didn't have any).<br /> <br /> Also, the developers have explicitly not ruled out the possibility of Lunars developing Styles for use in distinctly non-human forms (much as how the Pterok can design a personal Style humans likely can't use). So you could have a Fog Shark Style designed entirely to be used in the form of a shark. It's just that the developers are not going to make such a thing FOR you, because it would be decidedly niche.<br /> <br /> <br /> But now that I've laid all that out, I want to explore the question in my mind which quickly arose from this issue. Namely, the forms of gods, elementals and demons.<br /> <br /> Spirits come in many forms, and not all of them humanoid! Many spirits will be much stronger than the mortal humans or beasts they resemble, whether thunder god or thunder <i>bird</i><i>.</i><br /> <br /> If a Lunar eats a thunder god and takes his shape, we presume that she can learn to use some of his divine powers by paying XP for them, just as she could do when mastering the tricks of her stolen mortal eagle shape. So when wearing his form, she could use those powers in addition to any Martial Arts she knows (since his form is humanoid), and quite possibly add any Martial Arts <i>he </i>knew by using his stolen memories as a mentor for her self-driven training.<br /> <br /> Now let us suppose she instead eats an elemental with the mind as well as the shape of a beast; the aforementioned thunderbird. It didn't know any Martial Arts, and the Lunar cannot perform any when using its shape. But the Lunar CAN invest XP into <i>two</i> different sources of power -- the elemental beast's animal form (as per the eagle's tricks) and the beast's elemental powers (as per the god's divine powers).<br /> <br /> Also, there's precedent with things like the Kukla and raksha behemoths for Exalted to support animal-minded creatures having higher stats and generally superior physical power compared to sapient characters. It's just &quot;in-genre&quot; for the dumb beast to have more brute power to throw around.<br /> <br /> Thus, even when moving up from mortal to divine forms, I don't see Lunars suffering from &quot;no MA as animals&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> Thoughts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 01-24-2015, 01:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-24T10:35:14-08:00","id":380285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/380264-so-if-lunars-can-t-use-ma-in-animal-forms-divine-person-forms-vs-divine-beast-forms#post380264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and quite possibly add any Martial Arts <i>he </i>knew by using his stolen memories as a mentor for her self-driven training.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is this/has this ever been a Thing, where taking Heart's Blood gives you memories? I don't think so but I could be forgetting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-24T10:39:43-08:00","id":380290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/380264-so-if-lunars-can-t-use-ma-in-animal-forms-divine-person-forms-vs-divine-beast-forms?p=380285#post380285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is this/has this ever been a Thing, where taking Heart's Blood gives you memories? I don't think so but I could be forgetting.</div> </div> </div> </div>There were Knacks and Charms for it in Second Edition, but they were either pitifully weak (Intimate Training Recollection) or so overpowered that they had to be balanced into near-uselessness (Lessons in the Blood), or locked behind elder minimums (Predator's Insight).<br /> <br /> <i>None</i> of them tried the middle ground of &quot;you can use the victim's memories in place of a tutor/mentor&quot;, which is something I hope to see in Third Edition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-24T12:31:35-08:00","id":380378,"title":"","content":"Sorry to just drop in for a nitpicky question, but I'm in a bit of a hurry. It's an interesting topic and I may have more to chime in about later.<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/380264-so-if-lunars-can-t-use-ma-in-animal-forms-divine-person-forms-vs-divine-beast-forms#post380264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In terms of crunch, we know that animals are going to have unique-ish abilities that they can unlock with XP.</div> </div> </div> </div>Have we actually heard that these will be unlocked with XP? We're talking about animals, here; they're not assumed to be PC material, so there's no reason to assume they have XP. I'd imagined animals are just kind of assumed to have them. With ST discretion, particular weakness or frailty in a specimen may be represented by missing some or having weaker versions, while great might by getting slightly buffed up versions (or maybe an extra option or two that makes sense). Not to say XP use for the sake of familiars or Lunars using animal forms is a bad idea at all,* but I'm curious where you heard them mention the idea. Might be a source of other quotes I'd missed, too.<br /> <br /> * I'm actually warming to it as a possible way for Lunars to specialize within shapeshifting. John's said several times that a Lunar can pick up an animal's shape for no XP, with an example cheetah for its crazy speed suggesting some/much of its capabilities would be already available, but that doesn't rule out a Lunar needing to invest a little more for particular capacities. Perhaps needlessly, I worry just a bit about every single Lunar getting a huge bag of tricks for no XP from animal shapeshifting. There's a(n again perhaps) needless concern that it might leave most Lunars feeling a bit too samey. Needing to invest a little XP to pick up particular animal capabilities would discourage it while not presenting an impossible obstacle for Beast Boy Lunars. This could of course also be countered by some Lunar Charms gearing themselves to buffing up animal capabilities (or maybe syngergizing with and/or getting extra functionality when in an appropriate animal's form).<br /> <br /> I could see either approach working, provided the splat's overall design bore it in mind from the word &quot;go.&quot; Part of me prefers the &quot;all animal capabilities for free, relevant Lunar Charms for specialization&quot; approach, though it's hard to say how much of that is inertia -- I'd nursed that expectation for a while. It's also possible the concern I hold isn't really a concern others or the devs see and thus isn't likely to be a factor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-24T12:39:24-08:00","id":380387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/380264-so-if-lunars-can-t-use-ma-in-animal-forms-divine-person-forms-vs-divine-beast-forms?p=380378#post380378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry to just drop in for a nitpicky question, but I'm in a bit of a hurry. It's an interesting topic and I may have more to chime in about later.</div> </div> </div> </div>I understand and look forward to your return.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Have we actually heard that these will be unlocked with XP? We're talking about animals, here; they're not assumed to be PC material, so there's no reason to assume they have XP. I'd imagined animals are just kind of assumed to have them. </div> </div> </div>NPCs in general don't have XP anyway, yet they do have traits which can increase with experience, such as Ability ratings and new Charms. These also happen to be traits that PCs can get by players spending XP.<br /> <br /> No, animal NPCs will not spend XP for the same reason that the Dragon-Blooded NPCs who hound your Solar PCs won't spend XP. But you can still use this purchasable traits to differentiate newbie Terrestrials from veteran Terrestrials, so it makes sense that an elder eagle might know some tricks that a fledgling wouldn't know.<br /> <br /> These are also traits that will reflect how much a Lunar PC has mastered the form, and a Lunar PC will have his player spend XP on those tricks.<br /> <br /> That is the understanding by which I base those assumptions.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm actually warming to it as a possible way for Lunars to specialize within shapeshifting. John's said several times that a Lunar can pick up an animal's shape for no XP, with an example cheetah for its crazy speed suggesting some/much of its capabilities would be already available, but that doesn't rule out a Lunar needing to invest a little more for particular capacities. Perhaps needlessly, I worry just a bit about every single Lunar getting a huge bag of tricks for no XP from animal shapeshifting. There's a(n again perhaps) needless concern that it might leave most Lunars feeling a bit too samey. Needing to invest a little XP to pick up particular animal capabilities would discourage it while not presenting an impossible obstacle for Beast Boy Lunars. This could of course also be countered by some Lunar Charms gearing themselves to buffing up animal capabilities (or maybe syngergizing with and/or getting extra functionality when in an appropriate animal's form). </div> </div> </div>Exciting, isn't it?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I could see either approach working, provided the splat's overall design bore it in mind from the word &quot;go.&quot; </div> </div> </div>Which we know the developers have taken the time and consideration to DO, this time. Animals and Lunars are being designed with each other actually in mind, rather than someone assuming it will all work out on its own.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-24T13:04:57-08:00","id":380404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd prefer a few int charms with the end result of &quot;X floating skill ranks, can use memories as tutor, and XP discount on certain abilities you can learn to use in that persons form&quot;(If you have to pay XP to learn that stuff&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, if you want to talk about about that, best to start a new thread. It's off topic here.<br /> <br /> This is not singling you out, Rater. If Zelb had posted again just to keep talking about the &quot;Heart's Blood memories&quot; tangent, I would have told him the same thing.<br /> <br /> A quick question-and-answer exchange is fine, but when someone goes beyond that, it's a derail.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-24T16:18:38-08:00","id":380540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay.<br /> <br /> I think that, in the form a Spirit be it god, elemental, or demon, The Lunar Should be able to learn some of it's Charms or other powers the same way they can learn &quot;Animal Techniques&quot; but only be able to use those charms in that form or a similar one.<br /> <br /> I don't think a Thunderbird Elemental or a Horse God should have the same potential for &quot;Animal Techniques&quot; as the Animals they represent, because they are not that Animal. Instead, since there's no such thing as a &quot;Generic&quot; spirit charm beyond the basic things that all spirits of one type can do, They Should Have Spirit charms that function similarly but not identically to those powers-probably in a way that makes them better than the &quot;Mundane&quot; form. (An Equinomorphic God of Racehorses should be able to race much faster than a mortal race horse, after all.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Firstly, the word for a horse-shaped being or object in English is actually hippomorphic (sort of like Japanese matching native for native and borrowed Chinese with borrowed Chinese, you're matching borrowed Greek with borrowed Greek, rather than with borrowed Latin). Secondly, there's no guarantee that any kind of spirit will have this same utility for Lunars. The word on the subject was that animal shapeshifting was going to be an awesome advantage, and giving even bigger boosts for non-animal forms would tend to undermine that. At best, the gods with that shape would get the same bonuses that Lunars would, and it would carry over to Lunars using the form, so that the divine shape would end up like a particularly strong beast.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I expect that most Gods will have either a humanoid form or the ability to assume one, and thus shouldn't be bared from Martial Arts unless their divine body is, due to their purview, to frail to preform the techniques.<br /> <br /> I Expect that most Elementals won't know Martial arts unless they posses Humanoid Form, like the Kings of the Forest, and thus I expect most Elemental forms will be bared from taking martial arts, unless the style was invented or designed for that Elemental.<br /> <br /> I expect that Demons might be able to use martial arts, but some of them may be restricted to certain styles-a Blood Ape is unlikely to be able to use any style that wasn't designed for a gorilla like shaped body.<br /> <br /> My preference would be, that if you can use the absorbed memories of a mortal martial arts master to tutor yourself in the style, that you'll be able to tutor yourself in a spirits powers in the same way, and in the animal techniques as well. </div> </div> </div>Charm-share took a major hit in EX3. If Eclipse Solars aren't absorbing everything, I doubt that we're going to be getting anything like the Lunar Knack to use spirit Charms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-24T19:36:22-08:00","id":380682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then what is the incentive to take non animal forms? One only needs to eat one or two gods to pose as a God, and one only needs to eat one or two demons to pass for a demon, and only one or two elementals to portray oneself as an elemental.<br /> <br /> If Lunars have no way to use the powers of a spirit, then there's no point in adding that spirit to their heartsblood, beyond disguises and you don't need more than a few for that. If not the charms, then what?<br /> <br /> Besides, I posited Animal formed spirits not having the same animal techniques as actual animals more because well, why would they have them? The God of Horses is no mere race horse, so why would he have the same powers as his inferior?</div> </div> </div> </div>The animals are being written as more than just alternate stat blocks for a reason. It's so that Lunars can do animal shapeshifting and have it be a big deal, so that they don't end up being written as a thematic slapdash for the third time. Focusing on other forms to the extent that they become better to have seems to be missing the point of Lunars. Don't be in a hurry to ditch beast forms and move on to the &quot;real deal&quot;, because I don't think that something like that is going to be a thing for EX3 Lunars. Get excited about turning into an aurochs to gore someone and then changing into a wolf to hunt down his friends. Be proud to stand on two bird feet and taunt the enemy as a crow. Savor the exquisite feeling of shifting into a tyrant lizard and wrecking an army's shit. You may have Charms to work other feats, but animal shapeshifting is supposed to be a very useful strength, not a stepping stone moving on to greater things. It's like how Infernals are no longer going to be thrust into an environment where their goal is to become Devil Tigers as soon as possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-24T20:19:06-08:00","id":380711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/380264-so-if-lunars-can-t-use-ma-in-animal-forms-divine-person-forms-vs-divine-beast-forms?p=380682#post380682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The animals are being written as more than just alternate stat blocks for a reason. It's so that Lunars can do animal shapeshifting and have it be a big deal, so that they don't end up being written as a thematic slapdash for the third time. Focusing on other forms to the extent that they become better to have seems to be missing the point of Lunars. Don't be in a hurry to ditch beast forms and move on to the &quot;real deal&quot;, because I don't think that something like that is going to be a thing for EX3 Lunars. Get excited about turning into an aurochs to gore someone and then changing into a wolf to hunt down his friends. Be proud to stand on two bird feet and taunt the enemy as a crow. Savor the exquisite feeling of shifting into a tyrant lizard and wrecking an army's shit. You may have Charms to work other feats, but animal shapeshifting is supposed to be a very useful strength, not a stepping stone moving on to greater things. It's like how Infernals are no longer going to be thrust into an environment where their goal is to become Devil Tigers as soon as possible.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Sure, but i'd also like to eat elementals and gods and demons so I can be an tyrant lizard with a demons roar, or an aurochs with the speed of wind. A tiger with claws of lightning and power over storms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-24T20:32:17-08:00","id":380720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Godjaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/380264-so-if-lunars-can-t-use-ma-in-animal-forms-divine-person-forms-vs-divine-beast-forms?p=380711#post380711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Sure, but i'd also like to eat elementals and gods and demons so I can be an tyrant lizard with a demons roar, or an aurochs with the speed of wind. A tiger with claws of lightning and power over storms.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you may be missing an essential point of the character type.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-24T21:29:01-08:00","id":380727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not saying that Spirit forms should be superior to animal/beast forms, I'm saying that their needs to be some incentive to use them.<br /> <br /> If you want to disguise yourself as a god for some reason, you only need one or two Gods in your library. If the taking of the Heartsblood of Spirits is to remain a thing, their must be a reason to use it.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a pretty significant potential use you're neglecting: a Lunar isn't always taking on a different form because its stats are better/different or it lends unique physical capabilities. If a Lunar gains the Heart's Blood of a mortal ruler, there's a very good chance the ruler's physical strengths don't factor into the Exalt's reasoning at all. The Lunar's instead turning into that ruler for all the social power that form can wield within that sphere of influence. Even if it's only a very short-lived experience and the character never uses that form again, it's not like that shape cost the Lunar any XP to acquire, and it offered some very serious gains for the time the Exalt cared about it.<br /> <br /> A god can occupy a similarly prestigious position, so the same principle applies. In a particular situation, a Lunar may not be interested in &quot;just any god,&quot; so much as, say, &quot;Telios, God of the South Wind.&quot; It's also probably noteworthy that there's a lot of variety among divinities. I feel that's neglected in trying to coast on some sort of baseline divinity clout from being any old god. Like, a priest-king of a nation that mostly imports its metal equipment and chiefly exports wheat may show some cursory degree of respect to a Lunar if she shows up in the shape of a god of the forge, but there's only so much to expect. He's going to lend much more deference if she looks to be a goddess of the harvest. Naturally, probably still less than if the Lunar makes the effort to become the specific goddess with whom the priest-king communes, but hey. It illustrates that there are upsides to having a wide array of divine shapes in one's possession, regardless of whether any powers come into it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","user":"Gaius","date":". 01-25-2015, 12:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-24T21:37:39-08:00","id":380729,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/380264-so-if-lunars-can-t-use-ma-in-animal-forms-divine-person-forms-vs-divine-beast-forms?p=380720#post380720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think you may be missing an essential point of the character type.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Shapshifters, Warriors, Tricksters, Shamans. Terrible and glorious god-bodies. Man with monsters inside, or Monsters with men inside. I think I have that about right?<br /> <br /> If I want my Lunar to adopt the shape a a tiger seemingly make of storms, whose breath is hail and claws are lightning, and whose footfalls cause earthquakes, I should certainly be able to.<br /> <br /> We've been told that the connection between Lunars and animals comes from the connection between Luna and Gaia, but Lunars are still shapeshifters, so if not animals, then what are they shapeshifting into?<br /> <br /> I'm also not saying Lunars should be able to do this straight out of char gen. Obviously combining identities and their powers is a much higher power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":393,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","user":"Godjaw","date":". 01-25-2015, 12:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-24T21:50:01-08:00","id":380734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Godjaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/380264-so-if-lunars-can-t-use-ma-in-animal-forms-divine-person-forms-vs-divine-beast-forms?p=380729#post380729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I want my Lunar to adopt the shape a a tiger seemingly make of storms, whose breath is hail and claws are lightning, and whose footfalls cause earthquakes, I should certainly be able to.</div> </div> </div> </div>We also have to keep in mind the extent to which <i>native Lunar Charms</i> are responsible for turning their mortal animal forms into divine beasts of legend.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-24T22:16:20-08:00","id":380753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Godjaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/380264-so-if-lunars-can-t-use-ma-in-animal-forms-divine-person-forms-vs-divine-beast-forms?p=380729#post380729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Shapshifters, Warriors, Tricksters, Shamans. Terrible and glorious god-bodies. Man with monsters inside, or Monsters with men inside. I think I have that about right?<br /> <br /> If I want my Lunar to adopt the shape a a tiger seemingly make of storms, whose breath is hail and claws are lightning, and whose footfalls cause earthquakes, I should certainly be able to.<br /> <br /> We've been told that the connection between Lunars and animals comes from the connection between Luna and Gaia, but Lunars are still shapeshifters, so if not animals, then what are they shapeshifting into?<br /> <br /> I'm also not saying Lunars should be able to do this straight out of char gen. Obviously combining identities and their powers is a much higher power.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;A tiger made of storms&quot; sounds like a kind of nebulous space between Dragon-Blooded and Lunars that neither one necessarily covers very well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-24T22:22:34-08:00","id":380754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/380264-so-if-lunars-can-t-use-ma-in-animal-forms-divine-person-forms-vs-divine-beast-forms?p=380753#post380753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;A tiger made of storms&quot; sounds like a kind of nebulous space between Dragon-Blooded and Lunars that neither one necessarily covers very well.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> When you have something that can steal the shapes of other things, don't be surprised when there's some overlap in powers. In this case, it's Elemental powers and animals. It only seems Dragonblooded because Dragonblooded are also in some fashion Elemental.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-25T01:40:07-08:00","id":380857,"title":"","content":"I think acquiring the shapes of other supernatural actors should be handled with a priority to not make the actual Lunar disappear. Also, considering likely balance considerations in the powers of other beings, well, we don't want acquiring the shapes of gods to be this Edition's version of &quot;all Lunars need to favour Martial Arts&quot; do we?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-25T06:39:39-08:00","id":380930,"title":"","content":"Well first, there has been no mention of taking the powers of gods, elementals, or demons. Personally, I'm also highly opposed to the idea. It sets a very dangerous precedent where playing a Lunar is all about eating people to cheat the system. Paying XP is not a good reason to learn a unique power of a god or demon. General spirit charms I could let go, but I would never allow a Lunar to take charms unique to a specific spirit. EX3 seems to be moving in a direction where, instead of getting super charms at elder levels, you develop your own unique charms. Personally, I think that makes for a more interesting game. I'm opposed to anything that allows someone else to just take someone's uniquely developed charms/powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","name":"TalosX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"588"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-25T07:22:29-08:00","id":380964,"title":"","content":"I like the idea that among a Lunar's stolen forms, he can count an elephant-sized eagle whose body courses with lightning.<br /> <br /> Not so much the idea of a Lunar who can assume the form of an eagle made entirely of lightning.<br /> <br /> Through shapeshifting and their power to control how others perceive them, a Lunar could fake being an entirely elemental or numinous being, especially if he's using a form that's almost there.<br /> <br /> <br /> So perhaps Lunars can steal the Heart's Blood of elementals and elementally-associated gods, but the forms he takes are solidly material flesh-and-blood. God<i>blooded</i> versions of the creatures he ate. The thunderbird as a mortal bird of unusual size and voltage.<br /> <br /> To the extent that a Lunar can mimic another creature's Charms, it might only be as far as the Eclipse Caste can go this Edition, with the specially tagged Eclipse-keyword Charms which were balanced for Exalted PC use.<br /> <br /> <br /> Again, Lunars are going to have their own Charms for making their animal forms legendarily beastly. They don't need the full compliment of a spirit's Charms to do that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-25T08:44:05-08:00","id":381034,"title":"","content":"The most important spirit power is becoming immaterial. Everything else either can be faked, or avoided through bluffing.<br /> <br /> Well, even immateriality can be bluffed. Materializing costs a lot of motes, so if the Lunar is posing as a naturally immaterial being who happens to be material at the moment, others can easily assume that the Lunar is a spirit who doesn't want to waste that expenditure by abandoning physical form at any given moment.<br /> <br /> And if the Lunar can find the entrance to a spirit sanctum, or enters Yu-Shan, Malfeas or the Underworld, the divide of material and immaterial ceases to matter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-25T10:17:40-08:00","id":381111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">General Spirit Charms are no longer a thing, and if a Lunar can't duplicate some of a spirits powers, then they can't pass themselves on as that spirit and taking that specific spirit's form becomes meaningless, because animal forms are automatically better than spirit forms because they have special techniques the Lunar can learn while the Lunar can't learn the special powers of a spirit form.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where is this said? In fact, Eclipse's are said to be capable of learning some of the more general spirit charms. So &quot;no general spirit charms exist&quot; is obviously a misnomer. Also, I'm fine if that can't learn those either. Lunars are not suppose to be about stealing spirit/demon powers. That's not even remotely their purview. Their shape-changing is suppose to be more keyed to animals then anything else. I seriously doubt the devs are going to break the game by allowing Lunars to eat their way to every power in existence.<br /> <br /> Also, do elementals even have hearts? Not trying to be nitpicky, I'm actually curious. Even elementals that look like creatures, I've always just pictured as an outward appearance. For example, a wood spider is essentially a large piece of living wood. It has no organs that I'm aware of. I don't remember enough off the top of my head to know &quot;how a Lunar would perform a heartsblood ceremony on elementals&quot;? For that matter, gods are just masses of conscious essence (over-simplified but true). Do they have hearts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","name":"TalosX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"588"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-25T10:27:35-08:00","id":381116,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/380264-so-if-lunars-can-t-use-ma-in-animal-forms-divine-person-forms-vs-divine-beast-forms?p=380857#post380857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think acquiring the shapes of other supernatural actors should be handled with a priority to not make the actual Lunar disappear. Also, considering likely balance considerations in the powers of other beings, well, we don't want acquiring the shapes of gods to be this Edition's version of &quot;all Lunars need to favour Martial Arts&quot; do we?</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a difference between some shapes being an attractive option (especially since shapeshifting itself necessarily includes an opportunity cost, in that you're not wearing a different shape that might also be useful) and locking in a major character decision from chargen because, efficiency-wise, there IS no other option.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1024-thesaurasaurus","name":"Thesaurasaurus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-25T11:05:46-08:00","id":381190,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Godjaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/380264-so-if-lunars-can-t-use-ma-in-animal-forms-divine-person-forms-vs-divine-beast-forms?p=380711#post380711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Sure, but i'd also like to eat elementals and gods and demons so I can be an tyrant lizard with a demons roar, or an aurochs with the speed of wind. A tiger with claws of lightning and power over storms.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/380264-so-if-lunars-can-t-use-ma-in-animal-forms-divine-person-forms-vs-divine-beast-forms?p=380720#post380720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think you may be missing an essential point of the character type.</div> </div> </div> </div>An aurochs that moves at the speed of wind sounds very Lunar-y. A tyrant lizard with a demon's roar sounds like a form of hybrid body arrangement. A tiger with claws of lightning sounds doable, but I'm not sure about 'power over storms.'","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-25T11:21:03-08:00","id":381211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TalosX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/380264-so-if-lunars-can-t-use-ma-in-animal-forms-divine-person-forms-vs-divine-beast-forms?p=381111#post381111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where is this said? In fact, Eclipse's are said to be capable of learning some of the more general spirit charms. So &quot;no general spirit charms exist&quot; is obviously a misnomer.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let's see if this helps.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EX3 What We Know Wiki Quote Spam</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>(Holden)</b><br /> New Eclipse anima power: No more Charmshare between Exalts via the anima power. Eclipses -do- retain the ability to learn certain magics of other sorts of supernatural beings, such as spirits-- there's a Keyword denoting powers they can pick up (generally flavorful ones such as the ability to walk on clouds or interrogate the sea to give up its secrets, which would help them in their role as walkers-among-all-courts). These shared Charms don't have a special price hike, since the fact that they're Eclipse-available means we already judged they weren't going to break anything in an Eclipse's hand, and with that in place, there's no reason to tax your fun.<br /> <br /> <b>(Holden)</b><br /> Spirits aren't going to get a universal Charm set in 3e, beyond a very few super-common basics like Measure the Wind.<br /> <br /> <b>(Stephenls)</b><br /> Spirit stat blocks are going to resemble the 2e spirit stat blocks that were published before Roll of Glorious Divininty I, i.e. all the Charms will have their descriptions right in the block, so you won't need to flip any pages to see what the hell the spirit can do. And I think the rest of the stats will be built on the quick character rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>There was some extra context I remember around those remarks, so here's the full thrust as I understand it. There are a few super-common general Charms for spirits like Measure the Wind. This is because it genuinely wouldn't make sense to just repeat the full mechanics over and over again for so many spirits. These Charms are <i>not</i> what they are talking about when they speak of Charms that an Eclipse can learn.* A spirit's particular Charms will now be described right in their write-up, and some will be marked as available to Eclipses if the writer decides it's appropriate. The Charms in the write-up will include both stuff that's pretty common among spirits of its type (harvest gods or particular sorts of elementals are likely to have some overlap, after all), as well as anything more particular to the individual spirit. The exact range of powers an Eclipse can pick up will vary, but based on that first quote, it does seem to be focused on flavorful stuff that will help with the &quot;walkers-among-all-courts&quot; shtick, not just anything and everything that wouldn't be mechanically/thematically broken.<br /> <br /> * Well, some of them may be. Even then, my guess would be that an Eclipse would be learning &quot;this spirit's version of X,&quot; which will likely differ from another spirit's. It probably won't be as potent as the nearest equivalent Solar option, though may have some minor quirks or interesting flavors. Like a wind god's version of Measure The Wind may involve actually measuring the look/flow of wind from a target (&quot;The black wind howls...&quot;), while a goddess of swords may be able to see and assess the quality of someone's &quot;blade of the heart&quot; or something.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, I'm fine if that can't learn those either. Lunars are not suppose to be about stealing spirit/demon powers. That's not even remotely their purview. Their shape-changing is suppose to be more keyed to animals then anything else. I seriously doubt the devs are going to break the game by allowing Lunars to eat their way to every power in existence. </div> </div> </div>Agreed on the focus. There may be some executions the devs can come up with that don't dilute the themes at work, but it'd be tricky territory.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, do elementals even have hearts? Not trying to be nitpicky, I'm actually curious. Even elementals that look like creatures, I've always just pictured as an outward appearance. For example, a wood spider is essentially a large piece of living wood. It has no organs that I'm aware of. I don't remember enough off the top of my head to know &quot;how a Lunar would perform a heartsblood ceremony on elementals&quot;? For that matter, gods are just masses of conscious essence (over-simplified but true). Do they have hearts? </div> </div> </div>The specific answer of whether they have hearts is either, &quot;No,&quot; or &quot;It depends,&quot; but it's also not the germane question it might appear to be. Where it's come up in prior editions, the rule's been that a Lunar doesn't literally need blood from a heart for an appropriate target that's lacking in blood or a heart. Just something analogous. The line in the Green Sun Child Knack is, &quot;Demons who do not have blood are still valid targets; the Lunar simply has to consume some part of their vital ichors or insides,&quot; (MoEP: Lunars, p. 133) while the one for Hearth and Flame Shell is, &quot;Ending the hunt requires the Lunar to consume some vital part of the subject\u2014for some elementals, this may cause the Lunar pain or harm,&quot; (MoEP: Lunars, p. 134). Alchemicals are likewise called out as valid human targets for a Lunar in a sidebar (MoEP: Alchemicals, p. 43).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","user":"Gaius","date":".  Missed half a sentence. 01-25-2015, 02:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-25T17:14:21-08:00","id":381447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1. Eclipses are not getting &quot;General&quot; Spirit Charms. They are getting Spirit Charms with an Eclipse Keyword. Every Spirit has it's own uniques chars now, beyond very, very, very general powers<br /> <br /> 2. Lunars are not &quot;Keyed towards animals more than anything&quot;. They are not the Animal Exalted. They are the shapeshifting Godbeast Exalted. They change into Animals most easily becuase Luna loves Gaia and Animals are part of Gaia's domain.<br /> Devouring a demon to take upon it's shape and powers is totally something that should be within the power of a shape-shifting godbeast that gains forms by eating creatures and taking their powers.<br /> <br /> 3. Lunars are totally about eating things to take their form and powers. That's the entire purpose of the Heartsblood Library.<br /> <br /> you can use it to pose as a King, but you can't use it to pose as a god if you can't use that god's powers, because eventually the people you're trying to con will wonder why you're not bringing the rains.<br /> <br /> and taking the shape of a Spirit has always been something Lunars can learn how to do, which means it'll probably continue to be something they can learn to do, and if they can learn to do it, there should be a reason to do it beyond situational uses.</div> </div> </div> </div>And yet all your comments boils down to not. There isn't a single comment anywhere from the devs saying Lunars are the &quot;simulate anyones powers&quot; exalt. Being a shapeshifter means taking anothers shape, and by definition it's physical characteristics. It does not mean you take it's unique magic abilities or charms. If you eat Ligiers heart, you could take his shape, but you can't access his powers. Why, he's a the prime soul for Malfeas, and some of his powers come from that. He's the Green Sun and some of his powers derive from that. He's also a 3rd Circle demon, and some of his powers derive from that station. None of those are inherent to his physical form. You'd get squat.<br /> <br /> Also, you state their any not general spirit charms and Eclipse's are getting a keyword. Then you state their are general charms which are &quot;very general&quot;. Did you even bother to read what you wrote. Saying that the general charms are very general and their might not be alot of them, yet they are still there. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","name":"TalosX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"588"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-25T17:35:48-08:00","id":381457,"title":"","content":"Hmm considering one needs special prep to permakill a third circle I'm now picturing a very awkward scene where a lunar using Ligier's shape to get something from a second circle (because there's not a lot of the who will question Ligier) getting confronted by a very irritated Ligier.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-25T20:07:37-08:00","id":381546,"title":"","content":"So, here's the deal about Lunars and getting other people's Charms.<br /> <br /> I dunno if they're gonna get it. It's not something I've talked with the devs about, because none of my preliminary drafts for Lunars involve that sort of stuff. I've got literally as much information as y'all do.<br /> <br /> The way that the Eclipse anima now works\u2014a small subset of spirit/exotic Charms that have been explicitly flagged as being okay for PCs to take, as opposed to an all-inclusive list with exceptions\u2014makes me, as a designer, feel about 1000x more comfortable letting non-Solars get access to those effects through appropriate ways. I can feel much more comfortable knowing that it's not going to unbalance anything, and if I need to check interactions, it's with the handful of Charms that have the Eclipse keyword, instead of the vast majority of Charms that have the Native keyword. The ultimate deciding factor is a creative one, whether Lunars <i>should</i> be able to internalize these Charms (I say yes, but my vote's irrelevant). If we do decide they should, actually implementing it would be great facilitated by Eclipse restructuring.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-25T20:15:54-08:00","id":381549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">if a Lunar can't duplicate some of a spirits powers, then they can't pass themselves on as that spirit</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't agree with this premise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-25T20:57:46-08:00","id":381564,"title":"","content":"Assuming Lunars aren't able to to use the charms or power of other beings, I think in my games I would allow them to &quot;fake&quot; it.<br /> <br /> For example, maybe they could freely stunt actions that draw on the spirit's concept. So if a Lunar ate a Thunderbird, she wouldn't gain Thunderbird charms necessarily, but she might be able to gain the ability to make their voice boom with thunder or summon up a small sprinkle of rain - not enough to have any mechanical effect. Whereas if she took the form of a Flame Butterfly, she might be able to make herself glow with fire or create sparks. Again, these wouldn't have mechanical effects (the sparks wouldn't set anything on fire and might sting a bit but couldn't inflict burns), but be more of a visual effect.<br /> <br /> So enough enough to make people believe that the Lunar was a Thunderbird or a Flame Butterfly, without actually giving her full on spirit charms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 01-25-2015, 11:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-25T21:06:48-08:00","id":381566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/380264-so-if-lunars-can-t-use-ma-in-animal-forms-divine-person-forms-vs-divine-beast-forms?p=381546#post381546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, here's the deal about Lunars and getting other people's Charms.<br /> <br /> I dunno if they're gonna get it. It's not something I've talked with the devs about, because none of my preliminary drafts for Lunars involve that sort of stuff. I've got literally as much information as y'all do.<br /> <br /> The way that the Eclipse anima now works\u2014a small subset of spirit/exotic Charms that have been explicitly flagged as being okay for PCs to take, as opposed to an all-inclusive list with exceptions\u2014makes me, as a designer, feel about 1000x more comfortable letting non-Solars get access to those effects through appropriate ways. I can feel much more comfortable knowing that it's not going to unbalance anything, and if I need to check interactions, it's with the handful of Charms that have the Eclipse keyword, instead of the vast majority of Charms that have the Native keyword. The ultimate deciding factor is a creative one, whether Lunars <i>should</i> be able to internalize these Charms (I say yes, but my vote's irrelevant). If we do decide they should, actually implementing it would be great facilitated by Eclipse restructuring.</div> </div> </div> </div>Makes sense. I also wouldn't take much issue with Lunars being able to learn Charms that have been approved for Eclipses, but &quot;they can learn anything from the shape&quot; feels quite a bit dicier to me. Not least because one issue with the old Eclipse Charmshare, pre-Native, was that every single spirit Charm needed to be written under the assumption that a PC could learn it. This is a problem because it a) makes statting up a spirit a more onerous process than it should be and b) prevents the writing of cool powers that would be A-OK in the limited context of just the spirit, but which could easily do brokenly dangerous things were they to get into PC hands.<br /> <br /> As with Eclipses, this could be worked around by introducing another Keyword to define powers that are okay for Lunars to learn and use in that spirit's shape. However, the viability of a Lunar-OK keyword would kinda depend on whether it already appears in the core book; if not, that ship's probably already sailed. And it's questionable whether it would pop up there, as it would depend on knowing about its mechanical interactions with a splat that hasn't been written yet. Even if it was considered, there's also a question of whether it's too much of a bother, adding an extra &quot;Is it okay for this second splat to have this?&quot; overhead check to the process. Ultimately, I feel creatures and spirits should be written with their own merits as the writer's chief concern; the accessibility of their powers by PCs should be a distant third.*<br /> <br /> * Interactions the written-up individual/creature is liable to have with other things in the setting should naturally come in at a close second.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-25T21:13:14-08:00","id":381569,"title":"","content":"I'm gonna add another vote here for the idea that, if Lunars can steal the forms of other powerful mystic beings, then they should have some means of faking that being's powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T02:27:12-08:00","id":381711,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure how far Lunars even need to be able to go with &quot;You thought it was Swan Dragon, but it was me, Lunar!&quot;. They should have some facility to emulate Dragon Blooded, is a more immediate concern. Why is faking gods important, and why is it important to be able to do so without the clever tricks con artists often use even when they can't do everything that person can do?<br /> <br /> Nor that they should particularly, indeed, be &quot;incentivized&quot; to gobble up gods beyond the normal incentives Exalts get to gobble up and defeat gods.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T04:33:11-08:00","id":381747,"title":"","content":"When we say faking their powers, what are we exactly talking about? A lesser elemental dragon's breath? The ability of Ahlat to confer blessings on the Royal Guard? The hardiness and hard hitting of Octavian? General plot device stuff? If you've stolen Ahlat's shape, does that mean your most severe exertions cause idols around Harborhead to shatter? How many of the powers of different supernatural beings are actually visually, as opposed to mechanically, distinguishable? How well understood are they even by their peers? Who is ever to say that in any given instance, you're not just using your powers in a manner to which the witness is not accustomed?<br /> <br /> Like, if you're a Lunar and you have the stolen form of Ligier before somebody who is unaware that Ligier is dead (and maybe he isn't, maybe you had sex with him or something), and you go about crafting something, how would that person know that the way you're doing it isn't within the scope of what Ligier could or would do? I mean, even in portraying the actual Ligier, I would portray his crafting ability as an expansive and complex thing which works in different ways for different applications, or depending on his mood, inspiration or experimentation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T04:57:55-08:00","id":381760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/380264-so-if-lunars-can-t-use-ma-in-animal-forms-divine-person-forms-vs-divine-beast-forms?p=381546#post381546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, here's the deal about Lunars and getting other people's Charms.<br /> <br /> I dunno if they're gonna get it. It's not something I've talked with the devs about, because none of my preliminary drafts for Lunars involve that sort of stuff. I've got literally as much information as y'all do.<br /> <br /> The way that the Eclipse anima now works\u2014a small subset of spirit/exotic Charms that have been explicitly flagged as being okay for PCs to take, as opposed to an all-inclusive list with exceptions\u2014makes me, as a designer, feel about 1000x more comfortable letting non-Solars get access to those effects through appropriate ways. I can feel much more comfortable knowing that it's not going to unbalance anything, and if I need to check interactions, it's with the handful of Charms that have the Eclipse keyword, instead of the vast majority of Charms that have the Native keyword. The ultimate deciding factor is a creative one, whether Lunars <i>should</i> be able to internalize these Charms (I say yes, but my vote's irrelevant). If we do decide they should, actually implementing it would be great facilitated by Eclipse restructuring.</div> </div> </div> </div>My main issue with inability to copy charms, as I see it, is that while animals like Tyrant Lizards have their special powers modelled as just &quot;special powers&quot;, a lot of spirits have traditionally had fairly basic physical traits like &quot;I am always on fire&quot; treated as Charms, and missing those is a fairly noticeable lacuna in a way that, say, Hurry Home or Measure the Wind isn't. For this reason I'm kind of waiting to see what spirits look like in 3e before I decide where I stand on it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T05:13:24-08:00","id":381781,"title":"","content":"I did enjoy playing Sapphire Rhea as a trickster who was esentially stealing access to Fair Folk magic via Shifting Wyld Tides.<br /> Losing that power isn't a deal breaker, it was just the icing on the cake for being someone who frequently beat Raksha at their own games like it was some weird hobby.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T05:44:22-08:00","id":381808,"title":"","content":"I may have missed it, did anybody else say that gods who exist primarily in animal forms shouldn't use Martial Arts Styles for the exact same reasons Lunars shouldn't?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T06:05:04-08:00","id":381828,"title":"","content":"Martial Arts in Exalted are as much about Essence and Enlightenment as physical prowess, and while it might be weird for a sentient whale or whale spirit to use Tiger Style, if they've learn how to manipulate their Essence to emulate the Essence of a tiger, I don't see why it's much of a problem to just let the whale use Tiger Style. <br /> <br /> If however, whales (and whale spirits and such) can't use &quot;human&quot; martial arts, presumably they would be creating their own styles? So if I wanted to introduce a whale spirit and make it a martial artist (because Kung Fu Narwhals are cool) with a very aggressive combat style, would I be expected to basically homebrew a new martial art style for this one NPC? Or would be assumed that the ST would just jump through the legalistic hoop and say, &quot;This whale spirit isn't actually using Tiger Style, it's using Angry Swordfish style which happens to be mechanically identical to Tiger Style, just with a different name, because I'm not going to write up an entire martial art style for one NPC.&quot;<br /> <br /> If it's expected that ST's will just be giving out the normal &quot;human-style&quot; martial arts to non-human NPCs as a shorthand for homebrewing unique styles for individual NPCs, then you might as well just let anyone be physically capable of learning any martial arts style, rather than restricting things due to semantics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T07:20:39-08:00","id":381947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/380264-so-if-lunars-can-t-use-ma-in-animal-forms-divine-person-forms-vs-divine-beast-forms?p=381808#post381808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I may have missed it, did anybody else say that gods who exist primarily in animal forms shouldn't use Martial Arts Styles for the exact same reasons Lunars shouldn't?</div> </div> </div> </div>Based on your word choices, I'm not sure you understand.<br /> <br /> Lunars can use human-designed Martial Arts just fine in human and war forms, because those Martial Arts were designed for humanoid forms. You can't use Snake Style Charms as a snake because a snake has no limbs. Dragon Kings are close enough to humans (and DBT Lunars) in form that they should be able to practice most if not all human Styles.<br /> <br /> By contrast, the Pterok-designed Dagger Wing Style would be inaccessible for any humans who do not possess wings. The Mosok-designed Black Tide Style might be impossible for any creature which cannot swim as easily as a Mosok.<br /> <br /> The developers are not going to write a Snake-Snake Style which is a Martial Art for a serpent to fight like a serpent, because that would be incredibly niche and an inefficient use of word count. But they said that they're not going to tell you that a snake spirit who has no humanoid form while yet possessing human-like intelligence cannot design Snake-Snake Style for her own use.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/380264-so-if-lunars-can-t-use-ma-in-animal-forms-divine-person-forms-vs-divine-beast-forms?p=381828#post381828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Martial Arts in Exalted are as much about Essence and Enlightenment as physical prowess</div> </div> </div> </div>But it's also as much about physical ranges of movement as about Essence and Enlightenment.<br /> <br /> A sapient whale cannot use the human Tiger Style for the same reason a tiger cannot use the human Tiger Style -- the style was made to be used in human form, and whales are even farther from human form than tigers are.<br /> <br /> But a sapient whale is intelligent enough to design a Martial Art which it CAN use with its own natural form.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T07:41:47-08:00","id":381965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/380264-so-if-lunars-can-t-use-ma-in-animal-forms-divine-person-forms-vs-divine-beast-forms?p=381947#post381947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But it's also as much about physical ranges of movement as about Essence and Enlightenment.<br /> <br /> A sapient whale cannot use the human Tiger Style for the same reason a tiger cannot use the human Tiger Style -- the style was made to be used in human form, and whales are even farther from human form than tigers are.<br /> <br /> But a sapient whale is intelligent enough to design a Martial Art which it CAN use with its own natural form.</div> </div> </div> </div>Humans do not naturally make the movements or have the power and abilities of a tiger. By watching the tiger, and internalizing those movements, a human can make certain movements that are patterned after a tiger, even if the human isn't capable of making those movements exactly like a tiger does. Putting these movements together, the human creates a martial art style and calls it, &quot;Tiger Style,&quot; because it's based off of the tiger. And if the human is enlightened and make charms, you now have Tiger Style charms.<br /> <br /> Then, there is this hypothetical whale. Just like the human, he observes a tiger, learns its movements and, even though it can't actually move like a tiger, it does learn how to make movements that are inspired by the tiger. Putting these movements together, the whale creates a martial art style and calls it, &quot;Tiger Style,&quot; because, again, it's based off of the tiger.<br /> <br /> At this point, what is the real difference between (Human) Tiger Style and (Whale) Tiger Style? If this whale were enlightened and created (Whale) Tiger Style charms, should those charms be radically different from the (Human) Tiger Style charms? Or would it be reasonable to say that, in channeling the Essence of the Tiger into a martial art style, both the human and the whale come to a similar <i>spiritual</i> understanding of the tiger (ie, the same charms), even if the physical actions they take are different?<br /> <br /> Fundamentally what this would mean is, while a whale couldn't teach a human (Whale) Tiger Style, because a human can't copy the movements of a whale mimicking a tiger, and a human couldn't teach the whale (Human) Tiger Style, because a whale couldn't copy the movements of a human mimicking a tiger, Tiger Style charms would be identical across species.<br /> <br /> While there are different paths to refining your Essence if you want to mimic and harmonize it with the tiger, there is only one result once you have done so, regardless of what path you took.<br /> <br /> That is one option.<br /> <br /> The other option is to say that the whale's Tiger Style has an entirely different charmset than the human's tiger style, and the two are entirely different and incompatible. But from a mechanical perspective, this is kind of a nightmare because it means as an ST, if you ever decide to introduce Kung Fu Narwhal, either you have to homebrew up an entirely new style with charms for this one NPC, or you just delete that rule and give it the human tiger style charms for the sake of expedience.<br /> <br /> *EDIT* But going back to the initial premise, a Lunar in a whale form can't use Tiger Style because his body is so different from a human's. So what if the Lunar decided to learn Tiger Style from that Enlightened whale? It seems the Lunar would now have a Tiger Style he can use in Whale form, as well as a Tiger Style he can use in human form, and logically the Lunar would be able to use all of his Tiger Style charms in both human and whale form.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 01-26-2015, 11:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T07:42:48-08:00","id":381966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/380264-so-if-lunars-can-t-use-ma-in-animal-forms-divine-person-forms-vs-divine-beast-forms?p=381760#post381760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My main issue with inability to copy charms, as I see it, is that while animals like Tyrant Lizards have their special powers modelled as just &quot;special powers&quot;, a lot of spirits have traditionally had fairly basic physical traits like &quot;I am always on fire&quot; treated as Charms, and missing those is a fairly noticeable lacuna in a way that, say, Hurry Home or Measure the Wind isn't. For this reason I'm kind of waiting to see what spirits look like in 3e before I decide where I stand on it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree.<br /> <br /> I really don't want Lunars to access Hurry Home for the same reason I'm sure it's not Eclipse-OK. It's just too abusable in the hands of an Exalt character.<br /> <br /> I've already talked about how Dematerialize is perhaps the most important spirit Charm a Lunar might want to learn to pass as a spirit, but even then I was able to point out how it might not be strictly necessary.<br /> <br /> But Charms which could be modeled purely as Physical Merits (what might have been mutations in previous editions) rather than Charms at all? It would be nice if Lunars could enjoy those while wearing the form.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T07:52:49-08:00","id":381973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">None of the &quot;Animal Techniques&quot; are innate properties of the beasts shape-otherwise you wouldn't have to pay XP to learn them.<br /> <br /> Lunars have had &quot;Absorb the Memories of a Heartsblood form on acquisition&quot; in multiple charms, which has nothing to do with physical form<br /> <br /> Don't know about 1E, but 2E had a knack that elet you absorb a forms <i>destiny</i> on acquisition, and destiny is not a function of physical form.</div> </div> </div> </div>Having memories is no where near having a beings unique charms/powers. The absorb destiny was one of those silly concepts that was born out of the ridiculous 2E power creep. I fully expect it to disappear in 3E. If a Lunar takes a Solar's heartsblood, she shouldn't have access to Solar charms. Why, well that Lunar doesn't have a spark of UCS to power him! Same goes for Ligier, and not being the principle soul of Malfeas AND a humanoind form of the Green Sun itself. Also, the Animal Techniques that you mentioned are physical capabilities of the creature, NOT metaphysical powers of the soul/spirit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Between the two, a Lunar being able to spend XP to gain the ability to use a spirit's charms or other powers in the specific form of that spirit or in a similar one makes perfect logical sense.<br /> <br /> Besides, once more, there is the simple case that if you can't use the powers of a spirit, then there's very little reason for a Lunar to take the forms of Spirits-just ad two or three of each kind to your library so you've got a convenient disguise.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's because your misunderstanding my usage of &quot;general spirit charms&quot;. Which, admittedly, is my own fault. When I say general spirit charms, I mean charms that all members of that class of spirit possess. For instance; a charm that allows a thunderbird to cloak itself in lightning and deal lightning damage whenever it attacks or is attacked and is possessed by all thunderbirds, I consider this to be a general charm for this spirit. I'm fine with a Lunar learning this. However the ability of Ligier to manifest a Green Sun in the sky to make an area of Creation like Malfeas, is absolutely NOT something a Lunar should ever be capable of even in Ligiers form!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">And as has been said, you can't pose as a Spirit unless you have that spirit's powers Otherwise, people will wonder why the rain god isn't bringing the rain to the crops or why the city god can't tend to his city.</div> </div> </div> </div>Highly debatable. You could easily use sorcery to assist with the rain, and I don't know what &quot;tend his city&quot; means. I don't know of any charm that lets a city god &quot;tend his city&quot;. Though basic maintenance could be handle with Craft/Bureaucracy/Occult charms. Remember that Night Caste Solars are very good at impersonating others with disguise charms, and yet they can't steal peoples faces and memories as well as Lunars. If you can't think of a crazy alternative to simulate some of X gods or Y demons powers, then you're probably not cut out for the spy business anyways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2103,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","user":"TalosX","date":". 01-26-2015, 10:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","name":"TalosX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"588"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T08:10:19-08:00","id":381984,"title":"","content":"Absorbing someone's Destiny doesn't contribute to ridiculous power-creep. Checking your victim's star to see if he's dead is something a Sidereal can be reasonably expected to do!<br /> <br /> Being able to benefit from the astrological blessings that a Sidereal placed on your victim is a neat trick (and balanced against the possibility of having to suffer an astrological curse).<br /> <br /> Further, it meshes with the idea of &quot;the world itself thinks I'm that person&quot;, which means their personal belongings believe they belong to you. Including their attuned daiklaive and its socketed hearthstone, and the manse on the other end of that stone.<br /> <br /> Which is powerful, yes, but not overpowered. Since you killed that guy, you can already take and attune to his stuff. This just lets you skip the time it would normally take you to form that attunement.<br /> <br /> <br /> No one has ever said that Flickering Star Infusion is a viable method for gaining a Solar's Charms, though. That would be stupid.<br /> <br /> People are only talking about Lunars being able to learn the Charms which are natural to the species of creature they ate. A Solar is a human, but a human is not a Solar. Ligier's Charms come from being Ligier, but a Solar's Charms do not come from being human.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T09:07:04-08:00","id":382052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/380264-so-if-lunars-can-t-use-ma-in-animal-forms-divine-person-forms-vs-divine-beast-forms?p=381984#post381984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Absorbing someone's Destiny doesn't contribute to ridiculous power-creep. Checking your victim's star to see if he's dead is something a Sidereal can be reasonably expected to do!<br /> <br /> Being able to benefit from the astrological blessings that a Sidereal placed on your victim is a neat trick (and balanced against the possibility of having to suffer an astrological curse).<br /> <br /> Further, it meshes with the idea of &quot;the world itself thinks I'm that person&quot;, which means their personal belongings believe they belong to you. Including their attuned daiklaive and its socketed hearthstone, and the manse on the other end of that stone.<br /> <br /> Which is powerful, yes, but not overpowered. Since you killed that guy, you can already take and attune to his stuff. This just lets you skip the time it would normally take you to form that attunement.</div> </div> </div> </div>If that's all it does, then it might be alright. Truthfully I'm not to familiar with this charm. I remember it existing, but not the context of what all it did. I'd be careful of the &quot;their personal belongings believe they belong to you&quot; though. It sounds suspiciously like you might want to use his Evocations, and unless you pay for them, that's gotta be a no go.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/380264-so-if-lunars-can-t-use-ma-in-animal-forms-divine-person-forms-vs-divine-beast-forms?p=381984#post381984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No one has ever said that Flickering Star Infusion is a viable method for gaining a Solar's Charms, though. That would be stupid.<br /> <br /> People are only talking about Lunars being able to learn the Charms which are natural to the species of creature they ate. A Solar is a human, but a human is not a Solar. Ligier's Charms come from being Ligier, but a Solar's Charms do not come from being human.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're quibbling words here that I can do too. You can't access Ligiers charms because you're not a 3rd Circle Soul or Principle Soul of Malfeas. You can't access Ligiers charms because you are not a massive green sun. Ligiers power comes from the fact that he IS those things. Lets reverse things here. If you remove a Solar exaltation from a person, they no longer have access to Solar charms, makes sense right. If another demon overthrew Ligier and removed him as the principle soul of Malfeas, would his charms remain unchanged? I'd say no, part of this power and authority stems from that station. To support this, the Devs specifically said that a Deathlord could destroy a 3rd Circle Demon, but that a 3rd Circle Principle Soul would probably be a very even fight. It implies that Principle Souls get at least some of their power from their status as the favored soul.<br /> <br /> EDIT: BTW, Ligiers race as a demon in no way explains some of his incredible charms. If your talking about accessing basic charms that all demons have, then that's fine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2103,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","user":"TalosX","date":". 01-26-2015, 12:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","name":"TalosX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"588"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T09:31:09-08:00","id":382101,"title":"","content":"I think the issue of a whale using Tiger Style should be bound by the much more pertinent issue that I'm trying to imagine what it looks like, and it looks fucking dumb.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T09:53:22-08:00","id":382115,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/380264-so-if-lunars-can-t-use-ma-in-animal-forms-divine-person-forms-vs-divine-beast-forms?p=382101#post382101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the issue of a whale using Tiger Style should be bound by the much more pertinent issue that I'm trying to imagine what it looks like, and it looks fucking dumb.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sorry... I LoL'd! I needed it though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","name":"TalosX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"588"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T10:40:51-08:00","id":382133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/380264-so-if-lunars-can-t-use-ma-in-animal-forms-divine-person-forms-vs-divine-beast-forms?p=381760#post381760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My main issue with inability to copy charms, as I see it, is that while animals like Tyrant Lizards have their special powers modelled as just &quot;special powers&quot;, a lot of spirits have traditionally had fairly basic physical traits like &quot;I am always on fire&quot; treated as Charms, and missing those is a fairly noticeable lacuna in a way that, say, Hurry Home or Measure the Wind isn't. For this reason I'm kind of waiting to see what spirits look like in 3e before I decide where I stand on it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wrote or helped with all the spirit characters in the corebook. The kind of thing you're thinking of is now detailed as a Merit, rather than a Charm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T12:27:46-08:00","id":382203,"title":"","content":"Consuming a god's purview makes even less sense than consuming an Exalt's Exaltation.<br /> <br /> An Exaltation and a purview are separate from an individual's Destiny. Gods are assigned purviews, which affects their Essence, but their purviews do not grow out of their Essence.<br /> <br /> The River God is not the river.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T12:41:52-08:00","id":382209,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why not?<br /> <br /> I figure that to pose as a God, one must be able to convincingly portray themselves as having powers that are related to or influence that God's Domain.</div> </div> </div> </div>They probably can fake it well enough with their own native powers or other effects. It's not like the Lunar is going to step into that role permanently becoming the god. The point of this would more likely be to get information and support for a particular goal, and then leave. I don't think the Lunar needs to be able to fully take on that god's role, powers and all, to accomplish that.<br /> <br /> Do you really think mortals are going to go around demanding gods prove that they are who they say they are? If you do, you're not thinking in the right mindset re how mortals and spirits interact.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">And this is basically why I think, that Lunars should have a charm that let's them learn to duplicate a Spirit's Charms while in that Spirits form.<br /> <br /> If you can consume a God's Destiny, then you should be able to, with effort, learn to consume it's portfolio, and if you can absorb it's memories, then you should be able to consume it's memories of what it felt like when it was using it's power over it's portfolio, and between the two you should theoretically be able to duplicate some of those powers.<br /> <br /> Raslatedly, if you consume a Third Circle Demon, and it's destiny, then an othercharm should let you jack it's connection to it's proginator Yozi and use it to use some of it's charms(I imagine that this should be a speerate charm to the one that lets you use the charms of a God)</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe take a moment to consider that you're advocating for Lunars to have something on the level of 2e Eclipsoid Charmshare. Maybe re-evaluate your position, given how terrible Charmshare was from any kind of balance standpoint.<br /> <br /> The goal should never be &quot;Lunar can totally eat and permanently replace this god&quot; because that does some really weird things to the setting, and to the place of Lunars within it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T12:58:03-08:00","id":382218,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/380264-so-if-lunars-can-t-use-ma-in-animal-forms-divine-person-forms-vs-divine-beast-forms?p=382133#post382133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/380264-so-if-lunars-can-t-use-ma-in-animal-forms-divine-person-forms-vs-divine-beast-forms?p=382133#post382133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My main issue with inability to copy charms, as I see it, is that while animals like Tyrant Lizards have their special powers modelled as just &quot;special powers&quot;, a lot of spirits have traditionally had fairly basic physical traits like &quot;I am always on fire&quot; treated as Charms, and missing those is a fairly noticeable lacuna in a way that, say, Hurry Home or Measure the Wind isn't. For this reason I'm kind of waiting to see what spirits look like in 3e before I decide where I stand on it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wrote or helped with all the spirit characters in the corebook. The kind of thing you're thinking of is now detailed as a Merit, rather than a Charm.</div> </div> </div> </div>See this makes sense to me. If it's a merit of a physical attribute, then yes a Lunar should get that when he takes the critters Heartsblood. Even allowing Lunars to learn the charms that are &quot;Eclipse&quot; tagged should be fine, as Vance stated earlier that they were specifically balanced for PCs to take.<br /> <br /> Lunar shapeshifting into Gods/Elementals/Demons should be an option, but it needs to be balanced within the game. Eclipse's in 2E learning anyone's charms caused them to be massively unbalanced. We don't want to see Lunars go down that road. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","name":"TalosX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"588"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T14:55:58-08:00","id":382342,"title":"","content":"One way I have often used, either as part of the capacity to assume god/demon/elemental/et cetera shapes or as a separate knack that augments the others,is to be able to &quot;tint&quot; your Lunar Charms so they look like the kind of power a being of that shape might have. Claws of the Silver Moon as an earth elemental might look like stone or rock claws or massive hammer fists, Cunning Porcupine Defense as Ligier might manifest as piercing spikes of green light, or perhaps arcs or green flame. That sort of stuff. Good for fooling many people, but rising suspicions from anyone well-familiarized with that being's actual powers","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T14:58:08-08:00","id":382343,"title":"","content":"Come to think of it, it really seems like Lunars have a big problem with patiance. It's like they can't stay concentrated long enough to make a long-term goal worthwhile. Like, their crafting charms and such are supposed to revolve around building simple but efficient things on the fly or while on the move, their shapeshifting is limited in how long they can maintain a ruse, meaning that indefinite infiltration is impossible, their tactics are very much about roaming around the place, either gathering up new hoards of barbarians and efing' up somebody's shit, or using guerilla tactics to hit the Realm where it hurts. Even when they do stay for a long time in one place, they don't really seem to... Do anything. Raksi and Leviathan come to mind.<br /> <br /> Which, I don't think it's necessarily bad. If you ask me, there's a thematic space here, waiting to be explored. I want to see if this has something to do with their curse, or if it's further explored by their charms. Like, maybe their curse would make them fall into one of two extremes more and more- either a rampaging beast, or a hermit filled with ennui, that could be cool.<br /> <br /> About the &quot;assuming elemantal/god forms&quot; thing, I just wanna chime in and say that if Lunars don't have easy access to the spirit's powers, they better have charms that make it easier to fool people into thinking that they DO have these powers, lest we repeat the &quot;spy dillema&quot; from past two editions. You know, the one in which you first need Larceny, Dodge, Athletics and so on to be an effective rogue and be able to disguise as your target, then you need Presence and Socialize to impersonate them aaaand then you need the rest of the skills your target has to impersonate them well. Yeah, that one. Can we not have it again? Because I like spies, I might want to play as one. Can it please not be a silly gimmick?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2052,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2052-frombeyond","user":"FromBeyond","date":". 01-26-2015, 06:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2052-frombeyond","name":"FromBeyond","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"426"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T15:42:01-08:00","id":382393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TalosX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/380264-so-if-lunars-can-t-use-ma-in-animal-forms-divine-person-forms-vs-divine-beast-forms?p=382052#post382052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd be careful of the &amp;quot;their personal belongings believe they belong to you&amp;quot; though. It sounds suspiciously like you might want to use his Evocations, and unless you pay for them, that's gotta be a no go.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hadn't even considered Evocations, but no Lunar Charm should just let them <i>have</i> Charms, Evocations or Spells without paying for them.<br /> <br /> With the possible exception of Eclipse-OK Charms when wearing the victim's form. But I can easily see balance demanding Lunars pay for those, too. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You're quibbling words here that I can do too. </div> </div> </div>You're being more hostile than I feel is necessary.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You can't access Ligier's charms </div> </div> </div>I don't even want them. Not all of them, and certainly not the most powerful ones. Only the ones an Eclipse could learn, or which would be most important for pretending to be Ligier. <br /> <br /> But what Charms I <i>could</i> learn from him would stem from his Essence. An Exaltation is not human Essence, so a Lunar cannot learn Exalted Charms by eating humans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T17:21:24-08:00","id":382497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the [URL=&quot;http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/&quot;</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hadn't even considered Evocations, but no Lunar Charm should just let them <i>have</i> Charms, Evocations or Spells without paying for them.<br /> <br /> With the possible exception of Eclipse-OK Charms when wearing the victim's form. But I can easily see balance demanding Lunars pay for those, too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agree completely with this sentiment.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/380264-so-if-lunars-can-t-use-ma-in-animal-forms-divine-person-forms-vs-divine-beast-forms?p=382393#post382393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're being more hostile than I feel is necessary.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wasn't being hostile at all, at least that wasn't my intent. It was more of a &quot;snicker&quot; we could quibble words all day &quot;snicker&quot; situation. I apologize completely if my intent was misunderstood. I've never been the best at conveying my feelings in written form. Sorry about that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/380264-so-if-lunars-can-t-use-ma-in-animal-forms-divine-person-forms-vs-divine-beast-forms?p=382393#post382393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't even want them. Not all of them, and certainly not the most powerful ones. Only the ones an Eclipse could learn, or which would be most important for pretending to be Ligier.<br /> <br /> But what Charms I <i>could</i> learn from him would stem from his Essence. An Exaltation is not human Essence, so a Lunar cannot learn Exalted Charms by eating humans.</div> </div> </div> </div>The &quot;Eclipse&quot; tag is going to be interesting to see how it develops. What we know is that at least the charms with the tag have been specifically balanced for player use, so I don't have any issues with Lunars learning those. As for your final comment, a Demon's essence isn't human essence either. Now we're just quibbling again though! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2103,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","user":"TalosX","date":". 01-27-2015, 11:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","name":"TalosX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"588"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T19:17:11-08:00","id":382609,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I imagine that Lunar with the memory stealing charm who eats another Lunar to take their shapes might be able to learn Lunar Charms they don't already know as a result of doing so, but I don't think that's what you're talking about here.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree, and you're right.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T22:10:47-08:00","id":382746,"title":"","content":"Rater speaks my mind on the matter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T04:05:52-08:00","id":382904,"title":"","content":"The answer *could* well be &quot;As a Lunar Exalt, you craft a fraudulent cover story to explain this away, then use Charisma and Manipulation Charms, stunted sorceries and whatnot to seal the deal&quot;.<br /> <br /> If you're doing a &quot;The Talented Mr Ripley&quot; bit, murdering people and stealing their identities, then that, I think, should be most interesting when it involves actual deceptive skill and choosing your victims carefully and working out an exit strategy rather than just assuming their entire skillset by magic in the most literal way. (That's sort of close to what people complained about with Havesh, in the last thread - he doesn't seem to be applying any real skill a lot of the time).<br /> <br /> It may be hard to try and impersonate specific gods with particular kinds of miracles and attributes which cannot be faked through sorcery and supernatural blagging - maybe Lunar games will have to get by with having Lunars not impersonate those gods, not really a problem as there are an infinity of gods available on tap.<br /> <br /> But that's just one option.<br /> <br /> I personally have interest in Lunars and no real interest in Lunars who drink of and then take on the essence of other supernatural beings, like a sort of vampire of supernaturalism, parasitically leeching off other beings' supernatural strengths - such a group feels lame to me. Has a &quot;The Lunars is cosplaying another supernatural&quot; wannabee vibe. No effort, no skill, nothing that comes from within, nothing unique from your own character, just drinking up someone's milkshake and becoming an impostor. It would take a lot of skilled writing to push me away from that feel.<br /> <br /> Whether this is more of a turnoff than turnon is something which the team should be playtesting through with a group of playtesters who do not have any tendencies to become obsessively committed to one option or the other as &quot;rational&quot; or overridingly important at the expense of a bunch of perverse consequences or feel, or whatever, or too much prior experience with the game and splat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T04:39:07-08:00","id":382929,"title":"","content":"I'd like it to be an option.<br /> <br /> Like, if you want to play sexy dartfrog Lunar who rarely changes shape and just uses lots of poison and social charms and if she's in combat relies on being super fast and strong and having paralytic venom on her weapons? A paragon of human strength and speed and beauty, who can eat scorpions and wrestle bears and dance the sun up in the morning and sing songs to drive a whole town to orgiastic revelry? That should be valid.<br /> <br /> If you want to play her as someone who shapeshifts constantly, hunting down and murdering people and animals and altering her own spirit shape with the best of each stolen form? A peerless hunter who studies his prey and takes a lesson from each hunt he survives: the sting of the scorpion, the fangs of the cobra, the eyes of the eagle, the strength of the elephant? An ever-evolving beast gradually evolving into a mighty dragon of brilliant colors and feathered wings, with toxic spines and claws like sabers, a shifting-hued avatar of nature's fury? That should be valid.<br /> <br /> If you want to play her as someone who studies the occult, who poisons herself and goes on vision quests, who shapes the bright markings on her skin into sigils of terrible power, a shaman who learns the secret ways of the spirits, who studies the ancient languages of gods and demons...and then <i>hunts</i> them? A dread sorcerer who summons demons and orders them to flee, then pursues them through the jungle and devours their hearts to ritually steal their fell powers? A predator who stalks the lands of the dead and the halls of Heaven, luring stray spirits away from their fellows and consuming them, and adding their strange magicks to her own...and, perhaps, becomes more and more spirit and less and less flesh herself as she does so? That should be valid.<br /> <br /> You shouldn't <i>have </i>to play any of these characters! But I'd like you to be able to play any of the three. Hell, I'd like to be able to play any of the three as members of any of the castes, though of course of of them does fit best into one of the traditional molds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T04:51:33-08:00","id":382938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FromBeyond</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/380264-so-if-lunars-can-t-use-ma-in-animal-forms-divine-person-forms-vs-divine-beast-forms?p=382343#post382343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> You know, the one in which you first need Larceny, Dodge, Athletics and so on to be an effective rogue and be able to disguise as your target, then you need Presence and Socialize to impersonate them aaaand then you need the rest of the skills your target has to impersonate them well. Yeah, that one. Can we not have it again? Because I like spies, I might want to play as one. Can it please not be a silly gimmick?</div> </div> </div> </div>Larceny to be able to pass almost impermeably as somebody else and fairly well as a specific person is all well and good, but if you're going to pretend to be a swordfighter and then don't actually have any dots in Melee, then yes, you should be in a bit of trouble.<br /> <br /> At the same time, though, having that as an automatic invalidation of your disguise is just boring. You can still have tense scenes in which you try to bluff and bullshit your way around the apparent discrepancy, ala Inglourious Basterds.<br /> <br /> I think the milieu of a spy as you're imagining it is complex enough to warrant a diverse selection of Abilities, with an understanding that it isn't the sole way to spy. It's just weird to imagine a James Bond, or even Bridget von Hammersmark who have no dots in something like Socialize.<br /> <br /> For shapeshifting, again I would ask what kinds of powers specifically is any given mark supposed to have that could give the Lunar away?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T07:07:26-08:00","id":383043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wise Old Guru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/380264-so-if-lunars-can-t-use-ma-in-animal-forms-divine-person-forms-vs-divine-beast-forms?p=382929#post382929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd like it to be an option.<br /> <br /> Like, if you want to play sexy dartfrog Lunar who rarely changes shape and just uses lots of poison and social charms and if she's in combat relies on being super fast and strong and having paralytic venom on her weapons? A paragon of human strength and speed and beauty, who can eat scorpions and wrestle bears and dance the sun up in the morning and sing songs to drive a whole town to orgiastic revelry? That should be valid.<br /> <br /> If you want to play her as someone who shapeshifts constantly, hunting down and murdering people and animals and altering her own spirit shape with the best of each stolen form? A peerless hunter who studies his prey and takes a lesson from each hunt he survives: the sting of the scorpion, the fangs of the cobra, the eyes of the eagle, the strength of the elephant? An ever-evolving beast gradually evolving into a mighty dragon of brilliant colors and feathered wings, with toxic spines and claws like sabers, a shifting-hued avatar of nature's fury? That should be valid.<br /> <br /> If you want to play her as someone who studies the occult, who poisons herself and goes on vision quests, who shapes the bright markings on her skin into sigils of terrible power, a shaman who learns the secret ways of the spirits, who studies the ancient languages of gods and demons...and then <i>hunts</i> them? A dread sorcerer who summons demons and orders them to flee, then pursues them through the jungle and devours their hearts to ritually steal their fell powers? A predator who stalks the lands of the dead and the halls of Heaven, luring stray spirits away from their fellows and consuming them, and adding their strange magicks to her own...and, perhaps, becomes more and more spirit and less and less flesh herself as she does so? That should be valid.<br /> <br /> You shouldn't <i>have </i>to play any of these characters! But I'd like you to be able to play any of the three. Hell, I'd like to be able to play any of the three as members of any of the castes, though of course of of them does fit best into one of the traditional molds.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think anyone's saying you can't do all those things. What I've been saying is that if people think the Devs are going to let Lunar's take any Charm/Power of someone they eat, they're in for a very rude awakening. The Devs specifically went away from this with the &quot;Eclipse&quot; keyword. It's very unlikely that they're going to bring back that HUGE FAILURE know as &quot;charm-share&quot; to an entire splat! Vance specifically mentioned that not all Charms are designed for PC use, hence the &quot;Eclipse&quot; tag. I doubt they'd put such thought into it's development just to throw it out the window. So I'm sure what Charms/Powers that a Lunar can actual buy after eating a spirit/god/demon will also be specifically balanced for players. Now whether that means Lunars can only take Eclipse-tagged abilities, or they get a new Lunar tag, I honestly don't know. But I absolutely believe those powers will be balanced for player use.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","name":"TalosX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"588"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T07:32:18-08:00","id":383084,"title":"","content":"You were the one who suggested being able to make it rain by stealing the heart's blood of a god.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T07:40:30-08:00","id":383090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wise Old Guru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/380264-so-if-lunars-can-t-use-ma-in-animal-forms-divine-person-forms-vs-divine-beast-forms?p=382929#post382929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you want to play her as someone who studies the occult, who poisons herself and goes on vision quests, who shapes the bright markings on her skin into sigils of terrible power, a shaman who learns the secret ways of the spirits, who studies the ancient languages of gods and demons...and then <i>hunts</i> them? A dread sorcerer who summons demons and orders them to flee, then pursues them through the jungle and devours their hearts to ritually steal their fell powers? A predator who stalks the lands of the dead and the halls of Heaven, luring stray spirits away from their fellows and consuming them, and adding their strange magicks to her own...and, perhaps, becomes more and more spirit and less and less flesh herself as she does so? That should be valid.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel as though that sort of thing should serve as the learning and training basis of learning spells, some particularly weird Lunar Charms, or sorcerous workings.<br /> <br /> Actually, the last is probably the biggest one; it will probably be conceivable for a Solar to make themselves permanently capable of their spilt blood turning into scorpions without that being a Charm or otherwise undermining the Solar aesthetic.<br /> <br /> With Lunars, I think there's a fragile balancing point between maintaining the image of them having some qualities of hunters and devourers and gaining some face or power from the things they chase down, but not for the results to carry Lunars into the image of something else. I think the idea of actually getting Spirit Charms skews too far towards the latter.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T07:51:57-08:00","id":383105,"title":"","content":"Re: spies, if you do tend to try and impersonate the World's Most Amazing Man and you are not the most amazing man, that will perhaps not end that well.<br /> <br /> But! There is nothing forcing you to do that should you choose to play a spy. You can find a cover story that fits your talents - Lunars have a lot more options than others.<br /> <br /> Spies IRL, are for good reason, are backed by large organisations and specifically trained and coached. They do not assume people's identities whole cloth without being an uncannily close match to that person. Spy agencies manufacture identities and lay a lot of groundwork carefully to exploit and match the agent's actual skillset. They often choose naturally inconspicuous target identities for a reason.<br /> <br /> Having powers to help fool others into thinking the Lunar is a spirit, OK - the amount of additional magic you get to bridge the gap should probably not, by itself, have the effect of actually giving you more real capabilities, particularly not ones which can outgrow their function of helping you impersonate the target in question. <br /> <br /> If we end up with a case of &quot;To impersonate Raidan, God of Lightning, I must lightning...&quot; and this transforms into lightning becoming a primary method of attack or used to solve problems far removed from actually impersonating the lightning god, that can be an unintended consequence which could be a problem. Magic which is to help impersonate should have that function and be limited from use for any other function. It would need a fair amount of thought to do well.<br /> <br /> (Same for any Lunar magic from Social or Mental Attributes for emulating a person's skill.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wise Old Guru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/380264-so-if-lunars-can-t-use-ma-in-animal-forms-divine-person-forms-vs-divine-beast-forms?p=382929#post382929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd like it to be an option.<br /> ...<br /> If you want to play her as someone who studies the occult, who poisons herself and goes on vision quests, who shapes the bright markings on her skin into sigils of terrible power, a shaman who learns the secret ways of the spirits, who studies the ancient languages of gods and demons...and then <i>hunts</i> them? A dread sorcerer who summons demons and orders them to flee, then pursues them through the jungle and devours their hearts to ritually steal their fell powers? A predator who stalks the lands of the dead and the halls of Heaven, luring stray spirits away from their fellows and consuming them, and adding their strange magicks to her own...and, perhaps, becomes more and more spirit and less and less flesh herself as she does so? That should be valid.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm still not *that* interested in this type, but this is a lot more of an interesting way to spin the idea (I might be more easily persuaded here than I think).<br /> Specifically because she does draw that link between Lunars as gifted sorcerors and the sacrifice of spirits to gain sorcerous power, which is a generally in theme act for sorcerors (not just those who are Lunars).<br /> <br /> It feels closer to how sorcerors learn sorcery. It feels different from that idea of being guy who doesn't feel notable for his talent and doesn't use his skills, whose sole thing is to defeat a godbeast and eat its heart and impersonate it and leach off its style and identity in lieu of having his own Lunar style, skill, own personality as expressed through his Charms and sorceries and his own way of working.<br /> <br /> Main concern there would be more about that stream ending up having a transhuman feel and lacking human warmth or being an overpowered option.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T07:56:29-08:00","id":383109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which is a power necessary for posing as a Rain God. It may well be the only power of a Rain God.</div> </div> </div> </div>The hell it is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T08:01:05-08:00","id":383112,"title":"","content":"If I want to make it rain as a rain god, I'll learn sorcery.<br /> <br /> At most along that vein, wearing the form of a rain god might make casting the spell easier.<br /> <br /> Actually, we were told that there would be Charms which help you gather motes to cast spells... maybe Lunars can more efficiently cast spells when wearing a form appropriate to the spell. That would be neat.<br /> <br /> Also goes back to turning into Ligier. No, it doesn't give you his Total Annihilation-esque native power. But it... oh wait, that's Solar Circle. Lunars can't cast that. Oh well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T08:03:54-08:00","id":383116,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The hell its power necessary for posing as a rain god, the hell it's potentially the only power of a rain god, or the hell it's both?</div> </div> </div> </div>The hell it is, for both.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T08:41:11-08:00","id":383157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Who said anything about Lunars taking &quot;Any&quot; charm/Power?<br /> <br /> We're saying that they should be able to take <i>some</i> Charms or powers, and only from Spirits. Stop Strawmanning us.</div> </div> </div> </div>I take mild offense to claims that I'm strawmanning you. I've specifically said in several posts that some powers are probably good (aka those that have been properly vetted for players). My last 3 posts have all referenced the Eclipse friendly charms that were vetted for player use. You shouldn't take such a hostile tone, especially since I wasn't addressing any of your posts, but Wise Old Guru's post.<br /> <br /> As for taking &quot;specifically approved&quot; charms, that's not what you imply below:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">With a Demon, it's charms are manifestations of the fact that it's a demon-there's no Exaltation, nothing that fies away on death. You take it's shape, it's memories and it's destiny, and you take it's everything.<br /> <br /> It makes sense for a Lunar to take the Demons' charms if it can do all that, what you take is the entirety of the demon.<br /> <br /> Or, to explain the point, a Lunar wouldn't be able to take an Exalt's Charms because consuming the Exalts Heart's blood would not give it Exalt Essence, but <i>human</i> essence.<br /> <br /> Consuming the Heart's blood of a Demon, however, would give you that Demon's essence, and thus justifies being able to take that Lunars charms or other powers while wearing that demons form.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now maybe you meant &quot;a few specific charms&quot; of the devoured demon, but that's not what you said. Also as a minor nitpicking, you can't take a demon's destiny, because it doesn't have one. Destiny and Fate don't account for demons, fey, or denizens of the Underworld (their destinies ended when they died). Also, since we specifically mentioned him before, at least a part of Ligier's power stems from the fact that he is the Principle Soul of the Yozi Malfeas. Eating Ligier doesn't make you the Principle Soul, as that passes to another 3rd Circle Demon. You can't connect to the Yozi as one of his Souls... at least not unless you have a deep-seated desire to become an Akuma and puppet of Malfeas?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","name":"TalosX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"588"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T08:46:51-08:00","id":383159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which is a power necessary for posing as a Rain God. It may well be the only power of a Rain God.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's also, frankly, exactly the sort of charm that should have the keyword letting Eclipses/Lunars learn it. It's not like &quot;make it rain&quot; or &quot;make the crops abundant this year&quot; or &quot;make the river flood&quot; are particularly potent charms when compared to the native powers of the Exalted. If you're an Eclipse and the Rain Mother is your lover, perhaps she teaches you the song that summons the rains, or the dance which pleases the Sun and Moon and causes the clouds to part during monsoon season that they may watch. If you're a Lunar who eats the Rain Mother, maybe you can figure out the same tricks.<br /> <br /> The ones you don't want PCs learning are gonna be more about weird dice pools and mechanical interactions, I suspect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T08:50:28-08:00","id":383160,"title":"","content":"If Flickering Star Infusion should work at all on demons, raksha, or ghosts, it won't work as fully as for humans.<br /> <br /> I don't think any of them have stars that fall when they die, or that Sidereals can place astrological curses or blessings on them.<br /> <br /> A Lunar with Flickering Star Infusion should still be able to inherit (or share) ownership and attunement to a demon's, raksha's or ghost's possessions (artifacts, graces, grave goods, etc.*), but that shouldn't allow a Lunar to take a Second or Third Circle Soul's place within a Primordial's soul hierarchy.<br /> <br /> The Primordial and its soul should reflect each other. The Lunar cannot become a soul to make the Primordial reflect him unless the Primordial can impact him in turn. Establishing that kind of relationship should probably require a permanent and irreversible transformation into a demonic soul which costs the Lunar his humanity and Exaltation.<br /> <br /> <br /> * A victim's familiars and bonds with those familiars probably shouldn't count among their possessions, and neither any sapient servitors. You should need to persuade them to obey you (or fool them) yourself, though Flickering Star Infusion or a following Charm/Knack could probably HELP with that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 01-27-2015, 12:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T09:23:27-08:00","id":383224,"title":"","content":"I'm hard-pressed to imagine how you could possibly need the &quot;make it rain&quot; charm to pose as a rain god. You aren't generally going to be dealing with people who are in a position to demand you make it rain immediately -- it's quite possible that even if the rain god had that power, they virtually never used it. I guess if your boss comes around and tells you to make it rain, that could be an issue, but that's pretty unlikely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T09:28:21-08:00","id":383227,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/380264-so-if-lunars-can-t-use-ma-in-animal-forms-divine-person-forms-vs-divine-beast-forms?p=383160#post383160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If Flickering Star Infusion should work at all on demons, raksha, or ghosts, it won't work as fully as for humans.<br /> <br /> I don't think any of them have stars that fall when they die, or that Sidereals can place astrological curses or blessings on them.<br /> <br /> A Lunar with Flickering Star Infusion should still be able to inherent (or share) ownership and attunement to a demon's, raksha's or ghost's possessions (artifacts, graces, grave goods, etc.*), but that shouldn't allow a Lunar to take a Second or Third Circle Soul's place within a Primordial's soul hierarchy.<br /> <br /> The Primordial and its soul should reflect each other. The Lunar cannot become a soul to make the Primordial reflect him unless the Primordial can impact him in turn. Establishing that kind of relationship should probably require a permanent and irreversible transformation into a demonic soul which costs the Lunar his humanity and Exaltation.<br /> <br /> <br /> * A victim's familiars and bonds with those familiars probably shouldn't count among their possessions, and neither any sapient servitors. You should need to persuade them to obey you (or fool them) yourself, though Flickering Star Infusion or a following Charm/Knack could probably HELP with that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see any real issue with taking a spirit/demons possessions as your own. Even a Solar could kill Octavian and take his staff and eventually attune it to himself. You're advocating that a Lunar who ate Octavian could do the same thing, just speed up the process with a charm that makes the item think you've always owned it. That doesn't seem like a problem to me, though I'm not a Dev and have no say over such things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","name":"TalosX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"588"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T09:52:45-08:00","id":383247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/380264-so-if-lunars-can-t-use-ma-in-animal-forms-divine-person-forms-vs-divine-beast-forms?p=383224#post383224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm hard-pressed to imagine how you could possibly need the &quot;make it rain&quot; charm to pose as a rain god. You aren't generally going to be dealing with people who are in a position to demand you make it rain immediately -- it's quite possible that even if the rain god had that power, they virtually never used it. I guess if your boss comes around and tells you to make it rain, that could be an issue, but that's pretty unlikely.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also conceivable is a rain god who never could just make it rain on command, only increasing the possibility of rain over time. A Lunar devoting any effort at all to the charade could get away with a lot without much trouble by speaking authoritatively on the topic. Even a savant who's well acquainted with what rain gods can generally do would be aware that there are exceptions to the norm. Hell, even if said savant raised an issue, a sufficiently knowledgeable Lunar could always &quot;level with him&quot; using a different strain of deception for why she can't or won't use that power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T10:47:59-08:00","id":383331,"title":"","content":"I'd assume that if you're stealing the form of a prominent god or demon (or a specific mortal for that matter) you've got other shit to do than stand around proving you're the real deal. If I were playing a Lunar in the form of a god, and some upstart demanded I make it rain to prove my godhood, I'd lay into that mofo, using my native Lunar social Charms to convince him to shut up, go home, and think about what he's done.<br /> <br /> I don't really see Lunars getting a Charmshare-alike ability, even when they eat spirits. But I can see Lunars picking up packages of physical <i>merits</i> for each form they take. Most of the 'special powers' that animals get will come from merits. It's definitely not a stretch for the same mechanic that gives you a 'jaws that can bite a volkswagen in half' merit to also give you a 'always on fire' merit too, if you eat the right thing.<br /> <br /> Who knows, maybe you can have your own ST agree to give you minor cosmetic effects relating to the purview of whatever spirit you just ate, as a merit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Playing 3e and miss Anathema? Try my web app, <a href=\"https://www.lotcastingatemi.com\" target=\"_blank\">Lot-Casting Atemi</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/553-hushnowquietnow","name":"hushnowquietnow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar553_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"250"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T12:04:33-08:00","id":383398,"title":"","content":"I'm in favor of &quot;some spirit powers but not ALL spirit powers&quot;. Making all spirit charms effectively a subset of Lunar charms is a bad idea for the same reason as with Eclipses Mega-Manning everyone else into obsolescence, but really, what's the point of turning into a dragon if you can't even burninate some fools?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1024-thesaurasaurus","name":"Thesaurasaurus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T14:45:16-08:00","id":383613,"title":"","content":"There might still be ways to do that which aren't Charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T16:01:44-08:00","id":383731,"title":"","content":"This isn't the first time you've said such, but it's not particularly true here either.<br /> <br /> <i>Words have no &quot;exact&quot; meanings.</i> They're <i>always</i> colored by perceptions held by the people using them, colored by connotations and regional usage and professional jargon, and yes, even colored by the emotions you feel when you read or hear or say them.<br /> <br /> Words are not, cannot be, perfect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T19:54:11-08:00","id":383914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Note that the majority of the time I say &quot;some&quot; charms/powers.<br /> <br /> What I said in that one spcific instance does not invalidate what I've said in other instances, and I also said nothing, in that instance, about Lunars being able to learn all of a Spirits charms.<br /> <br /> If I don't say anything of the sort, then I can not be held responsible for you reading to much into my words.<br /> <br /> The exact wording is the only meaning to my words.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, so lets break this down so we can see where you say &quot;I&quot; made a mistake in reading to much into your words.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">With a Demon, it's charms are manifestations of the fact that it's a demon-there's no Exaltation, nothing that fies away on death. You take it's shape, it's memories and it's destiny, and you take it's everything.<br /> <br /> It makes sense for a Lunar to take the Demons' charms if it can do all that, what you take is the entirety of the demon.<br /> <br /> Or, to explain the point, a Lunar wouldn't be able to take an Exalt's Charms because consuming the Exalts Heart's blood would not give it Exalt Essence, but human essence.<br /> <br /> Consuming the Heart's blood of a Demon, however, would give you that Demon's essence, and thus justifies being able to take that Lunars charms or other powers while wearing that demons form.</div> </div> </div> </div>So your first two sentences you talk about taking the demon's shape, memories, destiny, and it's &quot;everything&quot;. Well probably not the best word usage on your part, but we'll let it go and move on.<br /> <br /> Your third sentence says it makes sense for a Lunar to at the Demon's charms after what you previously mentioned, because your taking the &quot;entirety of the demon&quot;. Hmm seeing a pattern hear, but lets continue.<br /> <br /> Your forth statement talks about not being able to take an Exalts charms for lack of the exaltation, I agree but that's not what we're hear debating at the moment.<br /> <br /> Lastly you state that taking the Demon's heartsblood and essence, that your justified in taking (I'm pretty sure you meant to write Demon there) the Demon's charms or other powers while in it's form.<br /> <br /> Okay so in your statements, you didn't once use a single phrase to tell readers you only meant some of the demon's charms, and not all. You did however use phrases like &quot;taking it's everything&quot; and &quot;take the entirety of the demon&quot;. I hope you can see how this is confusing. Now if I were alone in misinterpreting you, I'd apologize and move on. But several others have replied to your posts in this thread specifically because it looked like you were advocating a Lunar should get access to all spirit charms. Obviously your saying that's not your point of view. So we obviously don't have a point of contention at the moment.<br /> <br /> It is always on the writer to get his point of view across when writing for a group of people. That's what makes someone a good writer. Count Alucard is right that written word is always going to be imperfect on some levels, but you made some minor mistakes that completely altered the message you were trying to send. You shouldn't accuse someone of &quot;strawmanning you&quot; or say it's &quot;there responsibility for reading to much into your words&quot; when it was your literal words that spelled out my conclusion.<br /> <br /> I hope we can let this go now and both move on. Derailing this thread anymore when we apparently agree that only specifically balanced charms should be available to Lunar's is waste resources we could be investing in discussing other facets of Lunar's. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","name":"TalosX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"588"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T13:42:02-08:00","id":400806,"title":"","content":"So, bad news and good news, based on current discussion at RPG.net.<br /> <br /> <br /> Bad news is that Lunars may not be able to wear the forms, or perhaps even take the Heart's Blood, of spirits. (Which is not to say Lunars can't fake those forms or their powers!)<br /> <br /> Good news is that mortal animals are being designed to be so powerful and scary that, when combined with human intelligence and Lunar Charms, becoming an elemental beast wouldn't actually result in a significant improvement.<br /> <br /> The Lunar doesn't hunt the Nemean Lion; he IS the Nemean Lion. He is the Fenris Wolf, the Jormungandr, the Roc, the Orochi.<br /> <br /> If Lunars have to grow in power by buying Charms like other Exalted, that doesn't really seem like a problem to me. Lunars are Exalted, after all, and that's what Exalted do, and gaining the power to fly or swim or step on a house without XP is already a huge boon.<br /> <br /> Besides, even if I can't turn into a phoenix, I could always get magical tattoos to set my body on fire; which means I can be a fire-bear as easily as a fire-bird!<br /> <br /> <br /> Still, I'm pitching the question of Eclipse-OK Charms to Morke and Holden now, for clarification.<br /> <br /> And I'll ask if Heart's Blood is still on the table for stealing appearance, possessions and memories, if nothing else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 02-10-2015, 04:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T13:51:50-08:00","id":400818,"title":"","content":"It is indeed a good day.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T13:58:41-08:00","id":400824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/380264-so-if-lunars-can-t-use-ma-in-animal-forms-divine-person-forms-vs-divine-beast-forms?p=400806#post400806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bad news is that Lunars may not be able to wear the forms, or perhaps even take the Heart's Blood, of spirits. (</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know how to feel about this. Though it is probably for the best if allowing Lunars to take the forms of gods and demons opens up a huge magic can of worms in the way that 1e/2e Eclipse Charmshare did.<br /> <br /> If animals are significantly buffed to be interesting and useful, then I think that is more than good enough. As you said, a Lunar's own Charms probably lend themselves excellently to mimicking a true god for duplicitous purposes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T14:10:48-08:00","id":400832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though it is probably for the best if allowing Lunars to take the forms of gods and demons opens up a huge magic can of worms in the way that 1e/2e Eclipse Charmshare did.</div> </div> </div> </div> More than just that; it's all in the name of giving them clarity of theme and function. One of the best ways to help people get Lunars is being specific on what kinds of shapeshifters they are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T14:13:23-08:00","id":400836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/380264-so-if-lunars-can-t-use-ma-in-animal-forms-divine-person-forms-vs-divine-beast-forms?p=400832#post400832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> More than just that; it's all in the name of giving them clarity of theme and function. One of the best ways to help people get Lunars is being specific on what kinds of shapeshifters they are.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess, given precedent, it just seems <i>odd</i>. I'm not sure what this says about what kinds of shapeshifters they are, except &quot;they only turn into people and animals, and maybe also plants and terrain features.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T14:50:40-08:00","id":400866,"title":"","content":"Plants and terrain features are out to, and good riddance to them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T14:52:55-08:00","id":400868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/380264-so-if-lunars-can-t-use-ma-in-animal-forms-divine-person-forms-vs-divine-beast-forms?p=400866#post400866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Plants and terrain features are out to, and good riddance to them.</div> </div> </div> </div>It sounds like Lunars are &quot;the animal Exalted, except not because we don't want to call them that.&quot;<br /> <br /> I mean animals are cool especially with the new powers and all, but it feels a bit meh. Yes, they were all over the place in the past, but some of this just feels too <i>narrow</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T15:00:53-08:00","id":400876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/380264-so-if-lunars-can-t-use-ma-in-animal-forms-divine-person-forms-vs-divine-beast-forms?p=400868#post400868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It sounds like Lunars are &quot;the animal Exalted, except not because we don't want to call them that.&quot;<br /> <br /> I mean animals are cool especially with the new powers and all, but it feels a bit meh. Yes, they were all over the place in the past, but some of this just feels too <i>narrow</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even if 'animals' includes all kinds of people, insects, and prehistoric monsters?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T15:04:26-08:00","id":400878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/380264-so-if-lunars-can-t-use-ma-in-animal-forms-divine-person-forms-vs-divine-beast-forms?p=400876#post400876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even if 'animals' includes all kinds of people, insects, and prehistoric monsters?</div> </div> </div> </div>If shapeshifting primarily revolves around exploiting tons of animal-special-attacks, kinda? I mean, I'm sure it'll be very cool (and probably very Beast Boy/Vixen) in combat but outside of combat?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T15:11:33-08:00","id":400882,"title":"","content":"All right, some people should be reading the actual thread. <a href=\"http://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?745142-Exalted-Ask-the-Devs-pt2-(Hidden-Meaning-Behind-Veiled-Words-Style)/page274\" target=\"_blank\">Begin here</a> (and maybe work your way a bit back; it's not where the conversation begins, but it's where the strongest discourse does).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T15:11:40-08:00","id":400883,"title":"","content":"I was a large part in that discussion and the distinction they're making is that Lunars are not Animal Exalted because they don't emulate animals, they emulate animal myth. Memory like an elephant, not of an elephant. God-beasts, the super powers of animals, not &quot;things animals do&quot;<br /> <br /> I also am certain that they will be able to &quot;fake&quot; the more strange things with enhancing Lunar charms. For example, you might not be capable of becoming a ghost, but there may be a charm that augments your shapes to be ghost-like.<br /> <br /> These enhancing charms, along with the sheer amount of animals and combinations can lead to effective and weird forms.<br /> <br /> That said, i'll be damned if I can't DBT Kung-fu Panda.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":393,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","user":"Godjaw","date":". 02-10-2015, 06:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T15:17:31-08:00","id":400885,"title":"","content":"That link of Isator's is a good one. I'll drop in some quotes that strike me as especially pertinent. I may just quotedump everything John and Holden (and others?) have said on the topic around there later.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hatewheel, RPG.Net Thread</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I want to hit this sweet spot where a Lunar can say &quot;I'm smart <i>like</i> an elephant&quot; rather than &quot;I'm smart <i>as</i> an elephant.&quot; But I also want people to recognize that hey, animals are cool and turning into them has some genuine benefit. To a degree, the traits of animals and the things they can do have been further mythologized as well, so borrowing from them directly doesn't feel like a scientific down-turn but rather something that makes you this amazing god-beast who can run down gazelles, wrestle with lions, track like a tyrant lizard. But what I really want Lunars to impel toward is something ineffable, something that exists between the emphasis of animals, something not quite definite, very primal, fed by rage and instinct, and wholly something that belongs to and defines Lunars apart from everybody else.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> Lunars can co-opt the charge of a bull to smash down the mighty gates of Hashdur, and the scales of the alligator that let them soak up Essence from the warmth of the earth and the heat of the river.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> [EDITOR'S NOTE: In the context of Lunars learning the powers of other beings]<br /> There's also the probability of Lunars having better Charms than most of the things they look like, and having the power to sufficiently &quot;fake it&quot; on their own.</div> </div> </div> </div></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T15:23:41-08:00","id":400890,"title":"","content":"I'm actually kind of cool with the idea of transforming your body into a great tree or infusing your spirit into your land, to gain some form of mystic power (rather than just &quot;I wanna be a big tree&quot;).<br /> <br /> It just feels a lot to me like sorcerous ritual or spell and not really a Lunar Charm. I can imagine a sorceror or shaman from pulp or classily written high fantasy doing it. Just, not something Lunars can do with their body reflexively or naturally or simply. Doesn't feel Charm-y to me.<br /> <br /> Which maybe just means the whole idea that tattooed Lunars cannot shape their bodies and essence using sorcery very well should DIAF? Or do I need to *really* readjust my perceptions of what spells vs Charms feel like?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T15:36:34-08:00","id":400900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holden</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the things Geoff wrote in the outline for <b>Exalted: the Lunars</b> was that Lunars were not just shapeshifters, they were a particular type of shapeshifter. He had an entire separate attached document telling the writers how Lunar shapeshifting was going to work, what it did, what it didn't do, and how it did these things. This was an unusual measure for him, but he felt it was vital that all the writers on the book be on the same page from the word go about what kind of shapeshifters Lunars were or else they'd all walk in with wildly different assumptions and create a confused mess.<br /> <br /> Now, as all the world knows, the 1e Lunars book has a lot of problems, but the writers creating a confused mess with regards to Lunar shapeshifting was not one of those problems.<br /> <br /> In Second Edition, the <b>MoEP: Lunars</b> outline contains no such cautionary measures (I assume it was considered self-evident since the book was an update to already-published material), but MoEP: Lunars also took very decisive strides to move away from the 1e depiction of Lunars... and it did so, I think, without full consideration of what Lunars were going to be now. In other words, Second Edition was never sure what kind of shapeshifters Lunars were, or how far they were going to diverge from being the kind of shapeshifters they were in 1e-- nobody ever officially drew that boundary.<br /> <br /> The result was a confused mess, which is why this thread is full of people trying to argue for Lunars being werewolves, Beast Boy, the tulpa from It, Alex Mercer, Reed Richards, the Absorbing Man, Amazo, and more. 2e never made it clear what kind of shapeshifter they were supposed to be, and their scope kept creeping wider and wider in search of a solid identity as the edition went on.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThis makes a lot of sense to me, now I know that 3e Luanrs are going to go the way of 1e Lunars, insofar as there is a very specific focus for the tool of shapeshifting which is going to be spelled out for clarity ( and which 2e lacked) but I am still not sure I understand <i>what exactly that focus is specifically going to be.</i><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/380264-so-if-lunars-can-t-use-ma-in-animal-forms-divine-person-forms-vs-divine-beast-forms?p=400890#post400890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It just feels a lot to me like sorcerous ritual or spell and not really a Lunar Charm. I can imagine a sorceror or shaman from pulp or classily written high fantasy doing it. Just, not something Lunars can do with their body reflexively or naturally or simply. Doesn't feel Charm-y to me.<br /> <br /> Which maybe just means the whole idea that tattooed Lunars cannot shape their bodies and essence using sorcery very well should DIAF?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well yeah of course that should DIAF along with formlock and tattoos which require an air-breathing mermaid Charm to hide (versus having that as a built in effect).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":3420,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","user":"Zelbinnean","date":". 02-10-2015, 06:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T15:45:04-08:00","id":400912,"title":"","content":"I think something like &quot;face stealers, skin walkers, ravaging, unbowed, beautiful and cunning&quot; might be a good place to start. At least give a texture.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T15:50:42-08:00","id":400919,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/380264-so-if-lunars-can-t-use-ma-in-animal-forms-divine-person-forms-vs-divine-beast-forms?p=400866#post400866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Plants and terrain features are out to, and good riddance to them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed.<br /> <br /> Obviously there's some wiggle room for plants that move and attack and possibly even <i>think </i>like animals, but your run of the mill tree or flower was never worth turning into, and just dilutes the &quot;<i>Beast</i> God&quot; thing.<br /> <br /> And who needs to turn into a rock, if you can just <i>look </i>like a rock?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T15:53:53-08:00","id":400925,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/380264-so-if-lunars-can-t-use-ma-in-animal-forms-divine-person-forms-vs-divine-beast-forms?p=400890#post400890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm actually kind of cool with the idea of transforming your body into a great tree or infusing your spirit into your land, to gain some form of mystic power (rather than just &quot;I wanna be a big tree&quot;).<br /> <br /> It just feels a lot to me like sorcerous ritual or spell and not really a Lunar Charm. I can imagine a sorceror or shaman from pulp or classily written high fantasy doing it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oooh, good idea!<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Which maybe just means the whole idea that tattooed Lunars cannot shape their bodies and essence using sorcery very well should DIAF? Or do I need to *really* readjust my perceptions of what spells vs Charms feel like? </div> </div> </div>At least in my Creation, Tattoos will NEVER function like they did in previous ones.<br /> <br /> The transformation-blocking effect can, indeed, Die In A Fire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T15:54:34-08:00","id":400926,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/380264-so-if-lunars-can-t-use-ma-in-animal-forms-divine-person-forms-vs-divine-beast-forms?p=400919#post400919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And who needs to turn into a rock, if you can just <i>look </i>like a rock?</div> </div> </div> </div>But I thought &quot;Lunars are illusionists&quot; (in the vein of certain 2e Charms, e.g. Butterfly Eyes or the &quot;look like the person your target most wants//most expects to see&quot;) was also out as a Thing.<br /> <br /> (Which is disappointing to me if so, those were some of my favorite Charms for what they evoked).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T16:18:12-08:00","id":400971,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/380264-so-if-lunars-can-t-use-ma-in-animal-forms-divine-person-forms-vs-divine-beast-forms?p=400926#post400926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But I thought &quot;Lunars are illusionists&quot;... was also out as a Thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is, but there are ways.<br /> <br /> Turn into a creature that can disguise itself as a rock. Like an armadillo-beast with a rocklike shell, or an octopus that mimics the shape, apparent-texture and color of stone.<br /> <br /> Or use an artifact cloak, like the one the hobbits got in the Lord of the Rings Trilogy -- cover yourself completely, and you look just like a stone.<br /> <br /> Or cast a self-petrification spell.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">How was Spirit defined? Sometimes it includes Gods, Elementals, and Demons, while other times it's just Gods.</div> </div> </div> </div>Holden is looking askance at taking the Heart's Blood of anything that doesn't actually have a physical heart or blood in the same sense that mortal creatures do.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And I seriously think that plants that move and think might just bee wood elementals, so if SPirits includes Elementals, they're out. </div> </div> </div>&quot;Wood Elemental&quot; makes the most sense, but Creation always has more than one option for any concept.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So, if, big if, Lunars can take Spirit Forms, they can't copy powers, but thy might posses Native Charms that could let them pose as a supernatural creature outside of the things thy can take? </div> </div> </div>If they can't take a god's form, they could at least still mimic his appearance and have a shot at faking one or two of his powers. This was never really in doubt.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And the things they can take are &quot;Animals, including Dinosours and monsters we made up but that are non Supernatural&quot; &quot;Beasts, possibly like things from Greek Mythology like the Nemean Lion, but that just might be a lion totem Lunar whose invested points into evolving his Spirit Shape&quot; &quot;Humans, including things that are mostly human, such as beast men or certain other things&quot; And might include &quot;Creatures Twisted by the Wyld&quot;.<br /> <br /> Is that right? </div> </div> </div>Anything with a heart pumping blood through a mortal body, at least.<br /> <br /> I don't think Sea Cucumbers and Sea Sponges can rest easy just yet, though.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So in this Paradigm, Yammata no Orochi might have been a Snake Totem Lunar who managed to grow their SPirit Shape into an eight headed Godbeast? </div> </div> </div>Yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T16:23:57-08:00","id":400974,"title":"","content":"I'm not interested in becoming a giant tree, but infusing your spirit into the land sounds shaman-y.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T18:53:29-08:00","id":401256,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/380264-so-if-lunars-can-t-use-ma-in-animal-forms-divine-person-forms-vs-divine-beast-forms?p=400806#post400806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bad news is that Lunars may not be able to wear the forms, or perhaps even take the Heart's Blood, of spirits.</div> </div> </div> </div>You say that like it's <i>bad</i> news.<br /> <br /> Y'know, as opposed to &quot;the best thing I've seen re:Lunars this whole goddamned year.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T20:40:00-08:00","id":401392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/380264-so-if-lunars-can-t-use-ma-in-animal-forms-divine-person-forms-vs-divine-beast-forms?p=401256#post401256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You say that like it's <i>bad</i> news.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it's good news in terms of &quot;distilling Lunars down into their most Essential and punchy narrative&quot;.<br /> <br /> I just hope I don't lose all reason to Hunt spirits and take their Heart's Blood.<br /> <br /> Like I said, I want to be able to collect Heart's Blood in a variety of non-lethal ways, and use their blood against them in all sorts of ways. So that if I can't kill them in a fight (or can't afford for them to die yet), I can still get one over on them by completely changing the game to one that I can win.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-11T01:32:36-08:00","id":401627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not interested in becoming a giant tree, but infusing your spirit into the land sounds shaman-y.</div> </div> </div> </div> I'm not interested in becoming a giant tree, but I do like the image of a Lunar sitting amidst branches while the foliage very rapidly twines around them. Like a sloth covered with moss, for &quot;camouflage&quot;. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">But I thought &quot;Lunars are illusionists&quot; (in the vein of certain 2e Charms, e.g. Butterfly Eyes or the &quot;look like the person your target most wants//most expects to see&quot;) was also out as a Thing.</div> </div> </div> </div> There's more than one way to skin a rock. <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=PmDTtkZlMwM\" data-code=\"PmDTtkZlMwM\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/PmDTtkZlMwM/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-11T14:49:49-08:00","id":402515,"title":"","content":"So, What, other than people and animals, have hearts and blood?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-11T19:06:23-08:00","id":402772,"title":"","content":"Tell me a blood ape doesn't have blood, and I'll call you a liar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1419-wardragon","name":"WarDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1419_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1052"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-11T19:07:26-08:00","id":402773,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WarDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/380264-so-if-lunars-can-t-use-ma-in-animal-forms-divine-person-forms-vs-divine-beast-forms?p=402772#post402772\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tell me a blood ape doesn't have blood, and I'll call you a liar.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, that's usually someone else's blood, isn't it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-11T21:45:54-08:00","id":403005,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/380264-so-if-lunars-can-t-use-ma-in-animal-forms-divine-person-forms-vs-divine-beast-forms?p=401392#post401392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Like I said, I want to be able to collect Heart's Blood in a variety of non-lethal ways, and use their blood against them in all sorts of ways. So that if I can't kill them in a fight (or can't afford for them to die yet), I can still get one over on them by completely changing the game to one that I can win.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Remember that DotFA charm that lets a Lunar take a power of another character type by proposing and winning a contest or challenge of some sort with them? What if they could take Shapes the same way?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-11T21:49:16-08:00","id":403007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/380264-so-if-lunars-can-t-use-ma-in-animal-forms-divine-person-forms-vs-divine-beast-forms?p=403005#post403005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Remember that DotFA charm that lets a Lunar take a power of another character type by proposing and winning a contest or challenge of some sort with them? What if they could take Shapes the same way?</div> </div> </div> </div>I like it. Predation does not always have to be the literal predator-kills-prey situation. People are called &quot;card sharks&quot; and &quot;pool sharks,&quot; after all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-11T22:49:46-08:00","id":403054,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/380264-so-if-lunars-can-t-use-ma-in-animal-forms-divine-person-forms-vs-divine-beast-forms?p=403005#post403005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Remember that DotFA charm that lets a Lunar take a power of another character type by proposing and winning a contest or challenge of some sort with them? What if they could take Shapes the same way?</div> </div> </div> </div>I've thought it was a perfect new way to Hunt for Heart's Blood from the moment I heard of it.<br /> <br /> Not to mention that would be so much less broken than stealing someone's Charms.<br /> <br /> Vance also wrote a Charm where the Lunar can unilaterally steal Heart's Blood by prosecuting and winning a legal case against someone. Anyone remember that TV show with the defense attourney turned prosecutor, <i>Shark</i>?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-12T11:51:47-08:00","id":403558,"title":"","content":"What if Lunars can steal a still-living target's shape...and I mean really *steal*, not copy! The person now looks unremarkably average, as per the Innocous Merit, and is completely unrecogizable as their true identity, even by magical/astrological means. Maybe they even have some version of Arcane Fate, giving them penalties at convincing others they are who they say they are, esp. while someone else who clearly IS them is walking around...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-13T13:47:33-08:00","id":405021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/380264-so-if-lunars-can-t-use-ma-in-animal-forms-divine-person-forms-vs-divine-beast-forms?p=403558#post403558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What if Lunars can steal a still-living target's shape...and I mean really *steal*, not copy! The person now looks unremarkably average, as per the Innocous Merit, and is completely unrecogizable as their true identity, even by magical/astrological means. Maybe they even have some version of Arcane Fate, giving them penalties at convincing others they are who they say they are, esp. while someone else who clearly IS them is walking around...</div> </div> </div> </div>That doesn't sound like the Lunar brand of weird. Not visceral enough.<br /> <br /> Maybe an Abyssal, with his ghostly Underworld Solar magic, can do that, but a Lunar either eats you or rips your face off in order to wear your countenance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}